WEBVTT

00:04.917 --> 00:06.963
[heartbeat echoing]

00:14.014 --> 00:16.016
[heartbeat grows louder]

00:37.602 --> 00:39.604
[heartbeat continues]

00:58.493 --> 01:00.495
[heartbeat slows]

01:02.279 --> 01:04.846
[faint, muffled music playing]

01:04.847 --> 01:06.892
[slow, muffled thumping]

01:11.810 --> 01:14.464
[muffled music and thumping
grow louder]

01:14.465 --> 01:16.466
- [audio continues clearly]
- [both laughing]

01:16.467 --> 01:18.774
["Favourite Shirts [Boy Meets
Girl]" by Haircut 100 playing]

01:21.994 --> 01:24.692
- [rhythmic grunting]
- ♪ Boy meets girl... ♪

01:24.693 --> 01:26.216
DADDO:
Yeah! Come on!

01:28.305 --> 01:29.436
[shouts playfully]

01:29.437 --> 01:31.220
[Bela laughing]

01:31.221 --> 01:32.787
DADDO:
And don't puke on the judges.

01:32.788 --> 01:35.094
Whatever you do, Bela,
don't puke on the judges!

01:35.095 --> 01:36.226
MOMMY:
Knock, knock.

01:37.140 --> 01:38.401
Mommy!

01:38.402 --> 01:39.968
- Hi.
- DADDO: [sighs] Hey, love.

01:39.969 --> 01:41.361
- Hey.
- [song stops]

01:41.362 --> 01:43.798
This doesn't look like
bedtime to me.

01:43.799 --> 01:45.713
Yes, it does.
You're just never here.

01:45.714 --> 01:47.410
MOMMY:
I'm never here? Is that right?

01:47.411 --> 01:48.890
- Get in bed. Get off.
- [laughing] -DADDO: Come on.

01:48.891 --> 01:50.631
Mom's right, Dancing Queen.

01:50.632 --> 01:53.460
- Dive in there.
- Wait, I need Vulchy.

01:53.461 --> 01:54.809
MOMMY:
But you have Teddy. Come on.

01:54.810 --> 01:56.550
Really?

01:56.551 --> 01:58.769
Ugh. Are you sure? For bed?

01:58.770 --> 02:00.945
Vulchy's nice.

02:00.946 --> 02:02.643
The lady at the zoo said
vultures only eat

02:02.644 --> 02:04.688
stuff that's already dead.

02:04.689 --> 02:06.517
All right, baby.

02:09.346 --> 02:10.565
[Mommy boops softly]

02:11.783 --> 02:13.437
- Love you.
- BELA: Love you.

02:14.873 --> 02:16.744
DADDO:
Get some sleep.

02:16.745 --> 02:18.224
- [kisses] Night night.
- [sighs]: Okay.

02:18.225 --> 02:19.877
You want the door open?

02:19.878 --> 02:22.010
- A little bit.
- Okay.

02:22.011 --> 02:24.404
Night, Mommy. Night, Daddo.

02:24.405 --> 02:25.883
Night night.

02:25.884 --> 02:28.017
[door creaks softly, closes]

02:33.022 --> 02:34.893
[whispering]:
Good night, Other Mommy.

02:38.201 --> 02:40.768
I'm not sleepy yet.

02:40.769 --> 02:42.900
Can I keep playing with you?

02:42.901 --> 02:44.947
♪ ♪

02:54.783 --> 02:56.697
Other Mommy?

02:56.698 --> 02:58.700
[wind whistling softly]

03:17.197 --> 03:19.199
♪ ♪

03:28.556 --> 03:31.559
[door creaking]

03:56.627 --> 03:58.585
[eerie whooshing]

03:58.586 --> 03:59.716
[gasps]

03:59.717 --> 04:01.370
[voice shouts faintly]

04:01.371 --> 04:03.981
BELA:
<i>Hello and good morning.</i>

04:03.982 --> 04:08.204
My name is Isabela Martin.

04:09.292 --> 04:11.467
[grunts softly]

04:11.468 --> 04:13.252
And...

04:13.253 --> 04:16.646
this is "The Story of Me."

04:16.647 --> 04:18.692
♪ ♪

04:18.693 --> 04:20.694
I'm seven years old.

04:20.695 --> 04:24.306
I live with my mommy and Daddo,

04:24.307 --> 04:27.396
Russell Martin
and Ursula Martin.

04:27.397 --> 04:30.225
We are a very happy family.

04:30.226 --> 04:31.705
DADDO:
Louder. Louder.

04:31.706 --> 04:33.315
[high-pitched voice]:
We can't hear you.

04:33.316 --> 04:35.796
[New York accent]:
Why's she standing so weird?

04:35.797 --> 04:40.975
My hobbies are dancing,
books and animals.

04:40.976 --> 04:42.585
[Daddo growls playfully]

04:42.586 --> 04:43.673
[normal voice]:
Glasses. Looking good, Mommy.

04:43.674 --> 04:46.285
[chuckles] Thanks.

04:46.286 --> 04:48.069
I can't find my contacts.

04:48.070 --> 04:49.462
The sparkly case?

04:49.463 --> 04:50.854
Yeah. Have you seen them?

04:50.855 --> 04:53.161
Bela's practicing
her "Story of Me" speech.

04:53.162 --> 04:55.163
Oh, maybe I can hear it
when I come back.

04:55.164 --> 04:56.382
Thanks for doing breakfast.

04:56.383 --> 04:58.209
Can I be done now, please?

04:58.210 --> 04:59.602
Whole thing, miss.

04:59.603 --> 05:01.475
School's back next week.

05:03.041 --> 05:05.216
I don't want to talk
in front of my new class.

05:05.217 --> 05:07.218
I won't know anyone.

05:07.219 --> 05:08.698
Well, that's the point.

05:08.699 --> 05:09.830
We do this stuff now
so we're not scared

05:09.831 --> 05:11.222
when we're a grown-up.

05:11.223 --> 05:12.529
Hey, use the brave face
I gave you.

05:14.226 --> 05:16.619
- There it is.
- Something special about me

05:16.620 --> 05:18.360
is my zipper.

05:18.361 --> 05:20.884
I call it that because
it looks like a zipper.

05:20.885 --> 05:23.452
- MOMMY: Hmm.
- I got it climbing a fence

05:23.453 --> 05:25.367
when my mommy and Daddo were

05:25.368 --> 05:26.977
drinking wine
with their friends.

05:26.978 --> 05:28.849
Mm. Don't love that.

05:28.850 --> 05:31.112
Maybe let's pick another
special thing about you.

05:31.113 --> 05:33.201
- Yeah, or just don't mention
the picnic. -DADDO: Yeah.

05:33.202 --> 05:35.203
I should lie about it?

05:35.204 --> 05:36.944
- DADDO: No. Not lie.
- Uh... [laughing]

05:36.945 --> 05:39.381
Uh, maybe tell it
a little different.

05:39.382 --> 05:41.644
- It's a story.
- What's the difference?

05:41.645 --> 05:43.037
MOMMY:
Well, it just doesn't make

05:43.038 --> 05:44.995
Mommy and Daddo look like
good parents.

05:44.996 --> 05:47.520
Enjoy your breakfast,
my darling.

05:47.521 --> 05:49.304
[kisses]

05:49.305 --> 05:51.611
I'm gonna be home late again.

05:51.612 --> 05:53.090
Is that all right?

05:53.091 --> 05:54.962
Well, kind of has to be,
doesn't it?

05:54.963 --> 05:56.965
Uh, it doesn't.
That's why I'm asking.

05:58.706 --> 06:01.272
Yeah. Of course. Same team.

06:01.273 --> 06:03.057
- Okay. Same team.
- Yeah.

06:03.058 --> 06:04.667
- Love you.
- Love you.

06:04.668 --> 06:07.454
I got a ton of work
I should do anyways, so...

06:09.194 --> 06:12.196
[snoring softly]

06:12.197 --> 06:14.199
[Bela making
soft whooshing noises]

06:15.723 --> 06:17.725
[making playful noises]

06:20.467 --> 06:23.860
[descending vocalization]

06:23.861 --> 06:25.080
[imitates impact]

06:30.215 --> 06:32.216
Hmm.

06:32.217 --> 06:34.263
♪ ♪

06:54.544 --> 06:55.545
[chuckles]

07:06.861 --> 07:08.166
[chuckles]

07:09.646 --> 07:10.951
Whoa, whoa.

07:10.952 --> 07:12.997
[laughing]

07:17.828 --> 07:19.874
♪ ♪

07:23.138 --> 07:24.573
Yeah.

07:24.574 --> 07:25.967
Whoa.

07:27.185 --> 07:29.186
[squelching]

07:29.187 --> 07:31.233
[muffled creaking]

07:35.455 --> 07:36.672
[door closes]

07:36.673 --> 07:38.066
[keys clink]

07:42.331 --> 07:44.637
- Hey, sweetie.
- You're home.

07:44.638 --> 07:47.204
I thought I'd come home
and eat with you.

07:47.205 --> 07:49.032
- Where's Dad?
- He fell asleep in the office.

07:49.033 --> 07:51.208
- I'll go get him.
- No, no, no.

07:51.209 --> 07:53.646
Let him sleep.
He needs his rest.

07:53.647 --> 07:55.430
[gasps]

07:55.431 --> 07:58.564
Cookie dough ice cream
for lunch?

07:58.565 --> 08:01.175
What kind of mother would I be?

08:01.176 --> 08:03.786
[dishes clinking]

08:03.787 --> 08:06.223
How about scrambled eggs?

08:06.224 --> 08:08.183
We had that for breakfast.

08:10.446 --> 08:12.579
[sighs heavily]

08:14.145 --> 08:16.190
That's right. I forgot.

08:16.191 --> 08:18.279
How about pasta?

08:18.280 --> 08:19.672
Your favorite.

08:19.673 --> 08:21.804
I was wrong before
about your speech.

08:21.805 --> 08:24.504
You should always
tell the truth, no matter what.

08:26.636 --> 08:28.463
I won't lie.

08:28.464 --> 08:30.421
I love you
more than life itself.

08:30.422 --> 08:32.598
Did you know that?

08:32.599 --> 08:34.077
Yes.

08:34.078 --> 08:35.731
Do you love me that much?

08:35.732 --> 08:37.211
Yes.

08:37.212 --> 08:39.430
I like it when you say it.

08:39.431 --> 08:41.303
I love you, Mommy.

08:47.222 --> 08:49.832
Do you want to know
something silly?

08:49.833 --> 08:52.443
Okay.

08:52.444 --> 08:58.406
Sometimes I think about
when you and I were one person,

08:58.407 --> 09:02.585
and it makes me so happy I cry.

09:05.762 --> 09:07.023
Do you remember that?

09:07.024 --> 09:09.852
So I was a baby in your tummy?

09:09.853 --> 09:11.159
No.

09:15.772 --> 09:18.295
Do you remember
where you were before that?

09:18.296 --> 09:20.211
No.

09:21.212 --> 09:23.345
You were in my heart.

09:37.446 --> 09:39.447
[compass rattling]

09:39.448 --> 09:41.493
♪ ♪

09:45.628 --> 09:46.976
[gasps softly]

09:46.977 --> 09:48.848
[liquid bubbling]

09:48.849 --> 09:50.110
[sizzling]

09:50.111 --> 09:51.590
[rattling]

09:51.591 --> 09:53.593
♪ ♪

09:59.686 --> 10:01.991
[voice echoing]:
I want you to feel it, Bela.

10:01.992 --> 10:04.604
Can I go into your heart?

10:07.041 --> 10:08.477
I know it's you.

10:10.392 --> 10:12.437
[squelching]

10:15.005 --> 10:16.616
[echoing voice continues]:
I'm sorry.

10:17.834 --> 10:19.487
I thought you'd like this.

10:19.488 --> 10:22.012
You said you wouldn't
leave my room.

10:23.405 --> 10:25.276
You seemed lonely.

10:27.322 --> 10:29.541
Can I give you a hug?

10:30.717 --> 10:32.588
I don't want Daddo to see you.

10:34.155 --> 10:35.939
Are you mad at me?

10:38.159 --> 10:40.465
May I please be excused?

10:44.121 --> 10:45.645
Sure, sweetie.

10:49.605 --> 10:51.651
[slow footsteps]

10:58.396 --> 10:59.441
[gasps]

11:01.965 --> 11:03.967
[doors creaking]

11:11.279 --> 11:14.194
[panting softly]

11:14.195 --> 11:15.630
- [screams]
- Jesus.

11:15.631 --> 11:18.067
Let's go play outside.

11:18.068 --> 11:19.503
- What's that smell?
- Daddo, come on.

11:19.504 --> 11:22.071
- Hey, is the stove on?
- No, don't!

11:22.072 --> 11:24.160
[smoke alarm beeping]

11:24.161 --> 11:26.032
Oh! Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.

11:26.033 --> 11:28.077
Hey, get back! [groans]

11:28.078 --> 11:29.732
[exhales sharply]

11:30.733 --> 11:33.213
[water sizzling]

11:33.214 --> 11:34.780
[panting]

11:34.781 --> 11:36.869
[smoke alarm stops]

11:36.870 --> 11:39.219
Jesus. What were you cooking?

11:39.220 --> 11:40.524
I didn't mean to.

11:40.525 --> 11:42.222
I love you being independent,

11:42.223 --> 11:44.181
but you need a grown-up
to help keep you safe.

11:45.182 --> 11:47.141
- [shouts]
- [screams]

11:47.924 --> 11:49.970
Come on! Come on!

11:50.710 --> 11:53.060
Come on, Bela! Come on!

11:55.323 --> 11:57.106
[both grunting]

11:57.107 --> 11:58.891
Come on, come on.

11:58.892 --> 12:00.153
Go, go, go!

12:00.154 --> 12:02.069
♪ ♪

12:06.377 --> 12:07.900
- Thank you. -OFFICER:
Good night, Mr. Martin.

12:07.901 --> 12:09.466
- OFFICER 2: Good night.
- Sorry about this.

12:09.467 --> 12:11.251
- It's okay. We're here to help.
- [sirens wailing]

12:11.252 --> 12:13.166
- DADDO: I appreciate you all
coming out. -[Bela exhales]

12:13.167 --> 12:15.169
- [glass squeaking]
- [Bela humming a tune]

12:17.998 --> 12:19.607
- [quiet chatter]
- [dog barking in distance]

12:19.608 --> 12:21.088
[vehicle door closes
in distance]

12:24.439 --> 12:26.440
[Bela continues humming]

12:26.441 --> 12:28.138
[vehicle approaching]

12:36.103 --> 12:38.626
- What the hell happened?
- Somebody was in the house.

12:38.627 --> 12:41.237
- Oh, my God. Where's Bela?
- She's okay. She's in the car.

12:41.238 --> 12:43.022
- She's honestly better than me.
- MOMMY: Thank God you're okay.

12:43.023 --> 12:44.371
- DADDO: Hey, where were you?
- [panting]

12:44.372 --> 12:46.068
I was calling. I was texting.

12:46.069 --> 12:48.462
MOMMY: Oh, I didn't see it.
I'm sorry, I didn't know.

12:48.463 --> 12:50.246
DADDO:
I go in the kitchen, right?

12:50.247 --> 12:53.554
And under the counter,
there's a woman

12:53.555 --> 12:55.034
- tucked up in the fucking...
- What?

12:55.035 --> 12:56.731
...like, hiding. Yeah.

12:56.732 --> 12:58.080
Like she was fucking with me
or something. Just...

12:58.081 --> 13:00.648
- Are you stoned?
- No. No.

13:00.649 --> 13:02.258
It all happened superfast.

13:02.259 --> 13:04.434
I just grabbed Bela, and I ran.

13:04.435 --> 13:06.175
[sighs]

13:06.176 --> 13:08.090
Uh, I did a little in the
morning, but I swear to God.

13:08.091 --> 13:10.484
You didn't come home for lunch
or anything, right?

13:10.485 --> 13:12.835
MOMMY:
Of course I didn't. Why?

13:13.880 --> 13:15.620
She looked like you.

13:16.839 --> 13:18.840
- Bela, I said stay in the car.
- Honey.

13:18.841 --> 13:20.973
MOMMY:
Are you hurt? What happened?

13:20.974 --> 13:22.888
You don't have to be scared,
Mommy.

13:22.889 --> 13:24.367
She's nice.

13:24.368 --> 13:26.414
♪ ♪

13:37.120 --> 13:38.686
MOMMY:
Since your birthday?

13:38.687 --> 13:40.862
That's a long time.
Why didn't you tell us?

13:40.863 --> 13:42.211
BELA:
I don't know.

13:42.212 --> 13:44.039
We just play sometimes.

13:44.040 --> 13:45.998
And this isn't
some imaginary friend

13:45.999 --> 13:48.391
- that you and Dad created?
- BELA: No.

13:48.392 --> 13:50.176
Come on, tell me the truth.

13:50.177 --> 13:51.568
I am.

13:51.569 --> 13:53.614
She's really good at hiding.

13:53.615 --> 13:55.660
[low thunder rumbling]

13:57.271 --> 14:00.839
Okay. Where is Other Mommy from?

14:00.840 --> 14:04.408
I don't know.
She lives behind our doors.

14:13.853 --> 14:16.855
"Behind our doors."
What does that mean?

14:16.856 --> 14:20.597
Sometimes she's there.
Sometimes she's not.

14:20.598 --> 14:23.035
She can do magic stuff, too.

14:23.036 --> 14:26.255
Like grow really big,
grow really small.

14:26.256 --> 14:28.737
- [door opens]
- And make silly faces.

14:29.956 --> 14:32.958
Well, is she ever mean?

14:32.959 --> 14:34.829
Like, does she scare you?

14:34.830 --> 14:36.918
BELA:
Mm, not on purpose.

14:36.919 --> 14:38.137
She's still learning.

14:38.138 --> 14:40.966
We teach each other things.

14:40.967 --> 14:42.228
Like what?

14:42.229 --> 14:44.884
Carnations.

14:46.842 --> 14:48.148
MOMMY:
Flowers?

14:49.889 --> 14:52.194
Yeah. Sometimes.

14:52.195 --> 14:53.762
Okay.

14:59.289 --> 15:01.378
Why does Other Mommy
want to be here?

15:05.905 --> 15:08.385
Bela, we need to talk
about this.

15:09.996 --> 15:12.172
You smell like someone else.

15:13.173 --> 15:14.870
No, I don't.

15:16.132 --> 15:18.133
Bela, it's me.

15:18.134 --> 15:19.919
I'm Mom.

15:20.963 --> 15:22.791
Can just Daddo do bedtime?

15:26.751 --> 15:27.970
Yeah.

15:33.062 --> 15:34.934
[kisses, boops]

15:40.809 --> 15:42.680
It really scares me
when you talk like this.

15:46.249 --> 15:48.251
♪ ♪

15:49.861 --> 15:51.862
[rope creaking]

15:51.863 --> 15:53.909
[thunder rumbling softly]

16:00.263 --> 16:02.265
- [quiet snarling]
- [Bela gasps]

16:03.310 --> 16:05.051
[Daddo snoring]

16:07.879 --> 16:09.925
[snoring continues]

16:12.972 --> 16:14.974
♪ ♪

16:23.547 --> 16:26.985
OTHER MOMMY [whispering]:
Where shall we play tonight?

16:26.986 --> 16:30.206
[voice echoing]:
Should we go see the ocean?

16:33.209 --> 16:36.168
[whispering]:
Can I ask you something?

16:36.169 --> 16:38.475
Why do you have to go
inside my heart?

16:42.001 --> 16:44.220
To protect it for you.

16:46.179 --> 16:51.270
I help special children like you

16:51.271 --> 16:55.056
when their hearts are
about to be broken forever.

16:55.057 --> 16:57.059
[Daddo continues snoring]

17:02.195 --> 17:04.326
BELA:
But everything's fine.

17:04.327 --> 17:05.937
OTHER MOMMY:
Is it?

17:07.243 --> 17:10.594
It was your heart
that called to me.

17:12.161 --> 17:16.383
Deep down, you know something's
broken in this house.

17:17.601 --> 17:20.081
Don't you see?

17:20.082 --> 17:23.824
All you have to do is say yes,

17:23.825 --> 17:27.568
and everything will
stay magic forever.

17:30.049 --> 17:32.225
[whispering]:
What happens if I say no?

17:41.712 --> 17:43.278
Other Mommy?

17:43.279 --> 17:45.280
[breath hissing]

17:45.281 --> 17:48.284
["Butterfly" by Mega Bog
playing]

17:54.203 --> 17:55.857
[sputtering]

17:59.252 --> 18:00.948
DADDO:
No, seriously, Ruth.

18:00.949 --> 18:03.211
It's a long drive. We get it.

18:03.212 --> 18:05.039
[chuckles] I know.

18:05.040 --> 18:07.955
Yeah, you saved us from
having to clean the guest room.

18:07.956 --> 18:09.609
I don't want to do that.

18:09.610 --> 18:11.525
You want to talk to Ursula?
Hey, it's your mom.

18:12.569 --> 18:14.571
[balloon sputtering]

18:15.746 --> 18:17.182
Uh, Bela's here.

18:17.183 --> 18:19.706
Maybe we don't, uh,
tell Grandma about

18:19.707 --> 18:22.883
the Other Mommy thing
that other day?

18:22.884 --> 18:24.145
- Right?
- BELA: Why not?

18:24.146 --> 18:25.842
Because she'd want to meet it.

18:25.843 --> 18:27.540
Yeah. Um...

18:27.541 --> 18:28.889
[Daddo clears throat]

18:28.890 --> 18:30.325
Let's just keep it
a family secret

18:30.326 --> 18:32.327
until, you know,
you and I can see a doctor.

18:32.328 --> 18:33.546
- Sound good?
- Uh-huh.

18:33.547 --> 18:34.939
Okay. Here you go.

18:35.940 --> 18:37.289
Hi, Grandma.

18:37.290 --> 18:38.812
- GRANDMA RUTH: Bela.
- [doorbell rings]

18:38.813 --> 18:40.640
- How's everything going?
- I'm good.

18:40.641 --> 18:42.511
GRANDMA RUTH: Are you excited
for the party tonight?

18:42.512 --> 18:44.209
- DADDO: Kelvin.
- KELVIN: Hey, happy anniversary.

18:44.210 --> 18:46.385
DADDO:
Yeah. I thought we said 6:00.

18:46.386 --> 18:47.821
KELVIN:
Oh. Yeah.

18:47.822 --> 18:49.998
- Uh, my bad. My bad.
- DADDO: Cool. Bye.

18:50.999 --> 18:52.391
Babysitter's here!

18:52.392 --> 18:53.740
GRANDMA RUTH:
You should visit me soon.

18:53.741 --> 18:55.525
I'd love to spend
some time with you.

18:58.354 --> 19:00.399
I'm sorry I won't be
at the party.

19:00.400 --> 19:02.140
Why aren't you coming?

19:02.141 --> 19:04.794
Well, your mom thinks
anyone who didn't want to come

19:04.795 --> 19:07.536
to the wedding
shouldn't be there tonight.

19:07.537 --> 19:09.930
And I suppose I don't disagree.

19:09.931 --> 19:12.889
[chuckles]:
I've said too much.

19:12.890 --> 19:15.153
- You be good for your parents.
- I will.

19:15.154 --> 19:17.938
- Love you, Bela.
- Love you, Grandma.

19:17.939 --> 19:19.766
- MOMMY: Hey, Kelvin.
- Oh.

19:19.767 --> 19:21.637
You are late, buddy.

19:21.638 --> 19:23.335
You'll stay an extra 20 minutes.

19:23.336 --> 19:24.945
Sorry. For sure.

19:24.946 --> 19:26.164
Uh, where's Bela?

19:26.165 --> 19:28.036
I haven't seen her in hours.

19:29.298 --> 19:31.821
[chuckles] Okay.

19:31.822 --> 19:34.259
[singsongy]:
So she's hiding.

19:34.260 --> 19:35.608
Hmm.

19:35.609 --> 19:39.960
I wonder where she could... be.

19:39.961 --> 19:41.135
Ah!

19:41.136 --> 19:42.441
- [Bela imitates gunshots]
- Oh.

19:42.442 --> 19:44.312
- I got you.
- [dramatically]: Oh! Oh!

19:44.313 --> 19:47.272
I've been shot. Ow. [laughs]

19:47.273 --> 19:49.839
Hey, Bela, you want to fly?

19:49.840 --> 19:51.058
I'm too big.

19:51.059 --> 19:53.016
No, not for a wizard.

19:53.017 --> 19:54.888
Lifticus!

19:54.889 --> 19:57.499
[Bela and Kelvin
laughing, whooping]

19:57.500 --> 19:59.459
- [Bela squealing and laughing]
- [Kelvin growling playfully]

20:02.592 --> 20:04.594
- [lively chatter]
- [upbeat music playing]

20:14.822 --> 20:16.824
[cheerful children's song
playing quietly over TV]

20:18.826 --> 20:20.436
[Kelvin sighs heavily]

20:23.309 --> 20:24.961
You don't think that's enough?

20:24.962 --> 20:27.181
Can never be too sparkly.

20:27.182 --> 20:29.183
Oh. Right, right.

20:29.184 --> 20:30.576
Right, right.

20:30.577 --> 20:32.274
Yeah, well,
I'm definitely sparkly.

20:33.319 --> 20:34.754
[blows]

20:34.755 --> 20:36.017
[sighs]

20:41.457 --> 20:43.024
Hey, Kelvin.

20:45.548 --> 20:47.245
- Kelvin.
- Hmm? Yeah? Hmm?

20:47.246 --> 20:48.811
Can I show you something secret?

20:48.812 --> 20:50.987
Uh, sure.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

20:50.988 --> 20:53.208
I'm magic, too. Watch.

20:55.079 --> 20:56.950
- Wha-- Wait, wait, what?
- [light switch clicks]

20:56.951 --> 20:58.995
Okay. [blows]

20:58.996 --> 21:00.649
- Come on. I want to show you
something. -[chuckles]

21:00.650 --> 21:02.608
- What are you doing?
- Come on, Kelvin.

21:02.609 --> 21:05.001
What-- [chuckles] Okay.

21:05.002 --> 21:07.047
[straining grunt]

21:07.048 --> 21:09.571
- [exhales heavily]
- Hey, Kelvin.

21:09.572 --> 21:11.792
Don't tell Mommy and Daddo
you saw her.

21:13.881 --> 21:14.925
[chuckles]

21:17.363 --> 21:18.755
[door closes]

21:27.155 --> 21:30.289
[chuckles] Okay, what, uh,
what-what am I seeing here?

21:31.420 --> 21:32.639
Just be quiet.

21:35.859 --> 21:38.078
[whispers]:
Do you see her?

21:38.079 --> 21:39.820
[whispers]:
You're messing with me.

21:42.126 --> 21:43.345
[quiet squelch]

21:45.173 --> 21:48.089
♪ ♪

21:50.091 --> 21:51.614
- DADDO: Hey, party people.
- [gasps]

21:52.876 --> 21:56.183
Everything... normal in here?

21:56.184 --> 21:57.532
BELA:
Mm-hmm.

21:57.533 --> 21:59.055
You want to make
an appearance downstairs?

21:59.056 --> 22:00.143
Not really.

22:00.144 --> 22:02.015
Oh, come on, Bel-a the ball.

22:02.016 --> 22:05.149
Grown-ups have fun, too,
on certain weekends.

22:06.716 --> 22:08.935
♪ ♪

22:08.936 --> 22:11.894
["Into Black" by Blouse playing]

22:11.895 --> 22:13.941
[lively chatter]

22:17.205 --> 22:18.640
I'm in my pajamas.

22:18.641 --> 22:21.687
Yeah, but you're a kid.
Nobody cares.

22:21.688 --> 22:23.036
Here we go.

22:23.037 --> 22:25.691
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah... ♪

22:25.692 --> 22:27.301
WOMAN: The whole fucking world
is on fire.

22:27.302 --> 22:28.650
WOMAN 2:
My God, you're such a baby.

22:28.651 --> 22:30.913
WOMAN 3:
He doesn't love you.

22:30.914 --> 22:33.089
MAN: You ask enough times,
everyone says yes.

22:33.090 --> 22:34.656
[laughing]

22:34.657 --> 22:36.528
[laughter]

22:36.529 --> 22:38.399
WOMAN 4 [echoing]: Everything
is bullshit right now.

22:38.400 --> 22:40.706
- Yeah. Get it. I mean, you're--
- [Mommy laughing]

22:40.707 --> 22:42.969
- Come on.
- DADDO: Hey, you guys. Uh...

22:42.970 --> 22:44.753
- Hey. There he is.
- [laughs]: Hi.

22:44.754 --> 22:47.060
- Better half. How's it going?
- Hey, Bela, party girl.

22:47.061 --> 22:48.627
- Hey, buddy. Yeah.
- Yeah.

22:48.628 --> 22:50.019
Didn't know
you were gonna make it.

22:50.020 --> 22:51.456
- Yeah, yeah. Busy, busy, busy.
- Okay.

22:51.457 --> 22:53.632
- Heard about your little scare.
- Oh.

22:53.633 --> 22:55.024
- You heard about that?
- Yeah.

22:55.025 --> 22:56.200
That's... cool.

22:57.680 --> 23:01.683
Bela, can Uncle Frank get a hug?

23:01.684 --> 23:03.424
I know you're not really
my uncle.

23:03.425 --> 23:04.817
- [Uncle Frank chuckles]
- You're just Daddo's friend.

23:04.818 --> 23:06.732
Hey.

23:06.733 --> 23:09.169
You don't actually have to be
related to be family, okay?

23:09.170 --> 23:11.693
Listen, it's true. It's true.

23:11.694 --> 23:12.955
Fine.

23:12.956 --> 23:14.697
Can Regular Frank get a hug?

23:16.133 --> 23:18.221
All right, how about this?

23:18.222 --> 23:19.875
One high five,
I'm out of your hair.

23:19.876 --> 23:21.050
Come on. One high five.
Right here.

23:21.051 --> 23:22.704
Come on. Boom. Oh!

23:22.705 --> 23:24.576
MOMMY: You want him
out of your hair forever?

23:24.577 --> 23:25.925
- DADDO: All right.
- [Uncle Frank laughing]

23:25.926 --> 23:27.187
- Um...
- UNCLE FRANK: There you go.

23:27.188 --> 23:28.363
- Let's cut that cake.
- Yeah.

23:29.756 --> 23:31.757
I didn't sign up for this job.

23:31.758 --> 23:33.368
[lively chatter]

23:34.674 --> 23:36.457
Here we go. There we go.

23:36.458 --> 23:39.025
I'm moving as fast as I can.
Why don't you do it?

23:39.026 --> 23:41.288
Speech!

23:41.289 --> 23:43.377
Come on, speech!

23:43.378 --> 23:45.292
- UNCLE FRANK: Yo, big dog.
- Speech!

23:45.293 --> 23:46.554
UNCLE FRANK: You heard 'em.
They want you to say something.

23:46.555 --> 23:48.251
- Come on, you got to wow us.
- Speech!

23:48.252 --> 23:49.688
- I know, but don't.
What are you doing? -Yeah, no.

23:49.689 --> 23:51.559
Well, we said we weren't
gonna say anything,

23:51.560 --> 23:53.909
- but everybody's staring, so...
- [music and chatter quiet]

23:53.910 --> 23:55.998
- [chuckles] Uh, sorry.
- Brave face, Daddo.

23:55.999 --> 23:57.957
Uh... [chuckles]

23:57.958 --> 24:00.655
Uh, well, okay, sorry.

24:00.656 --> 24:02.875
Uh... sorry.

24:02.876 --> 24:07.270
Uh, we, uh, didn't do a
big thing when we got married.

24:07.271 --> 24:09.316
Uh...

24:09.317 --> 24:11.057
We, um... [smacks lips]

24:11.058 --> 24:12.841
We bought this house instead.

24:12.842 --> 24:18.847
We-we used that money wisely,
and... and, um...

24:18.848 --> 24:22.111
To be honest, this is
everything that I ever wanted,

24:22.112 --> 24:26.594
um, is to have a... a home
and-and to-to have a place

24:26.595 --> 24:28.727
that you could call home,
you know.

24:28.728 --> 24:32.644
And, um, this family
and this home,

24:32.645 --> 24:35.081
it's-it's...
it is everything to me.

24:35.082 --> 24:37.039
And, um... [smacks lips]

24:37.040 --> 24:40.478
But I know it's a choice, and I
know that it's hard sometimes,

24:40.479 --> 24:43.829
and-and I know, um,
there's, like, a million ways

24:43.830 --> 24:46.919
your life could go, obviously,
and, um, you know,

24:46.920 --> 24:48.747
I-I just want us to be happy
and, you know...

24:48.748 --> 24:50.662
I-- and we're so happy
to have everyone here

24:50.663 --> 24:52.925
- celebrating with us tonight.
- Yeah. Right.

24:52.926 --> 24:54.187
Right.

24:54.188 --> 24:56.145
Here's to
a cherished seven years.

24:56.146 --> 24:58.452
GUESTS:
Seven years!

24:58.453 --> 25:00.410
- Love you. All right.
- Love you.

25:00.411 --> 25:02.630
[music and chatter resume]

25:02.631 --> 25:04.502
And to Bela, my baby.

25:04.503 --> 25:07.201
I can barely remember
my life before you.

25:08.637 --> 25:12.161
Look, Bela.
Doesn't she look so pretty?

25:12.162 --> 25:14.860
I can't believe she's so big.

25:14.861 --> 25:16.470
All right, let's see you dance.

25:16.471 --> 25:18.124
She's actually really amazing.

25:18.125 --> 25:19.386
Come on, guys.

25:19.387 --> 25:20.996
- Bela!
- [overlapping chatter]

25:20.997 --> 25:23.259
Bela...
Come on, buddy. What's wrong?

25:23.260 --> 25:24.696
Hey.

25:24.697 --> 25:27.568
To Russ and Ursula, everybody.
Cheers.

25:27.569 --> 25:29.658
- GUESTS: Cheers!
- Cheers, cheers, cheers.

25:32.487 --> 25:33.619
- Bela.
- [door opens]

25:34.968 --> 25:37.317
- [door closes]
- [Kelvin imitates radio static]

25:37.318 --> 25:39.580
[Southern accent]: Uh, ma'am,
we've got you surrounded.

25:39.581 --> 25:41.147
Come out with your hands up.

25:41.148 --> 25:42.758
BELA:
I'll come out once I'm ready.

25:43.933 --> 25:45.020
KELVIN [normal voice]:
Okay.

25:45.021 --> 25:46.806
There anything I can do to help?

25:47.894 --> 25:49.982
BELA:
Make everyone go away.

25:49.983 --> 25:53.028
KELVIN:
Mm. I'll see what I can do.

25:53.029 --> 25:56.989
How... about... that?

25:56.990 --> 25:58.600
[chatter and music
stop abruptly]

25:59.862 --> 26:01.602
There you go. Huh?

26:01.603 --> 26:03.430
Party's over.

26:03.431 --> 26:05.301
BELA:
Really?

26:05.302 --> 26:06.694
KELVIN:
Yeah. Come on.

26:06.695 --> 26:08.479
Why don't you come see
for yourself?

26:10.569 --> 26:13.354
- [door creaking]
- [glasses clinking]

26:18.446 --> 26:20.491
[footsteps clinking]

26:30.850 --> 26:32.852
♪ ♪

26:35.332 --> 26:38.465
[voice echoing]: No one needs
that many friends anyway.

26:38.466 --> 26:39.554
Right?

26:41.643 --> 26:43.384
[breathes deeply]

26:44.428 --> 26:45.994
[voice echoing]:
Can we stay friends?

26:45.995 --> 26:48.519
Even once I get older?

26:49.912 --> 26:51.217
[chuckles]

26:51.218 --> 26:53.612
Oh, you mean
"if" you get older.

26:58.138 --> 27:00.269
[echoing voice continues]:
Hey, Bela.

27:00.270 --> 27:01.444
Want to fly?

27:01.445 --> 27:03.795
Come on.

27:03.796 --> 27:06.625
I didn't know
you could be Kelvin, too.

27:10.716 --> 27:12.631
I'll be whoever
you want me to be.

27:14.589 --> 27:16.547
That's too many fingers.

27:22.379 --> 27:23.642
[sharp crack]

27:29.256 --> 27:30.517
[screaming playfully]

27:30.518 --> 27:32.563
[both laughing]

27:35.479 --> 27:37.220
[screams]

27:39.005 --> 27:40.006
[gasps]

27:40.833 --> 27:42.356
[gasps]

27:44.793 --> 27:47.795
It's okay. I got you.

27:47.796 --> 27:49.188
I got you. Okay? Come here.

27:49.189 --> 27:51.190
It's okay.

27:51.191 --> 27:52.888
Come on. I've got you.

27:55.761 --> 27:57.240
There you go.

27:59.721 --> 28:01.287
[house creaking]

28:01.288 --> 28:03.681
I mean, it's fun, right?
Come on.

28:03.682 --> 28:06.422
[both laughing]

28:06.423 --> 28:08.338
You want to go see some more?

28:09.426 --> 28:10.600
I can't.

28:10.601 --> 28:12.994
I should probably get back now.

28:12.995 --> 28:14.648
[laughs]

28:14.649 --> 28:17.172
Aw, man. But, I mean,
I miss you so much though.

28:17.173 --> 28:19.479
And your parents don't care
at all when you're gone.

28:19.480 --> 28:20.872
- Yes, they do.
- No.

28:20.873 --> 28:22.744
Not like they should.

28:24.224 --> 28:25.921
Not like I do.

28:29.142 --> 28:32.187
I am going to miss you so much.

28:32.188 --> 28:35.234
- Aw, it's okay, Other Kelvin.
- [crying]

28:35.235 --> 28:36.365
I'll come back.

28:36.366 --> 28:37.715
[skin crackling]

28:37.716 --> 28:40.631
Bela, please let me
into your heart.

28:42.111 --> 28:45.070
It hurts so much, Bela.
I have to exist.

28:45.071 --> 28:48.029
[distorted]:
Please. You have to say yes!

28:48.030 --> 28:50.597
- Ow! Kelvin!
- [squelching]

28:50.598 --> 28:51.772
Stop!

28:51.773 --> 28:53.208
I'm sorry.

28:53.209 --> 28:54.950
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- [grunts]

28:56.386 --> 28:58.170
[gasps]

28:58.171 --> 29:00.303
[Bela panting]

29:01.043 --> 29:02.652
[grunts]

29:02.653 --> 29:05.004
- [squelching]
- [gasping]

29:09.965 --> 29:11.836
- Bela!
- [screaming]

29:11.837 --> 29:13.228
[distorted]:
Bela, I'm sorry.

29:13.229 --> 29:15.013
I'd never hurt you.

29:15.014 --> 29:16.841
Just say yes! Say it!

29:16.842 --> 29:18.320
- [explosion]
- MAN: Whoa.

29:18.321 --> 29:19.974
- [grunts]
- [guests gasping]

29:19.975 --> 29:21.454
[panting]

29:21.455 --> 29:24.022
- [concerned chatter]
- MOMMY: Bela? Bela?

29:24.023 --> 29:26.068
- BELA: Get away from me!
- [grunts]

29:28.636 --> 29:30.072
MOMMY:
Bela!

29:34.033 --> 29:35.295
Bela!

29:36.600 --> 29:37.905
What the hell's going on?

29:37.906 --> 29:40.169
[Bela panting]

29:42.606 --> 29:44.347
Honey, what's wrong?

29:45.566 --> 29:47.568
Is it really you?

29:52.878 --> 29:54.880
♪ ♪

29:56.272 --> 29:59.361
[chuckles]:
What? Baby.

29:59.362 --> 30:00.885
[screaming]

30:00.886 --> 30:02.887
[yelps]

30:02.888 --> 30:04.976
[chittering]

30:04.977 --> 30:06.152
[screaming]

30:07.544 --> 30:09.024
DADDO:
I'm coming!

30:10.330 --> 30:11.504
- [grunts]
- Oh, God!

30:11.505 --> 30:12.592
- [exclaims]
- Oh. Oh, God.

30:12.593 --> 30:14.463
Oh. Are you okay?

30:14.464 --> 30:16.291
I got you.

30:16.292 --> 30:17.902
Tell me what hurts.

30:17.903 --> 30:19.425
- I s-- I saw her.
- She's okay.

30:19.426 --> 30:21.427
[breath trembling]

30:21.428 --> 30:22.732
It w-- it was me.

30:22.733 --> 30:24.386
It w-- it w--

30:24.387 --> 30:26.259
It was m-me.

30:29.610 --> 30:32.090
Why the fuck was it me?

30:32.091 --> 30:33.308
[gasping]

30:33.309 --> 30:35.311
♪ ♪

30:36.530 --> 30:38.052
- Yeah, man.
- Thanks for having us.

30:38.053 --> 30:39.488
- Yeah, of course. Take care.
- [lively chatter]

30:39.489 --> 30:41.230
- Drive safe. Goodbye. -Bye.
- [rope creaking]

30:42.275 --> 30:44.885
They all think I'm crazy.

30:44.886 --> 30:47.106
Who gives a fuck
what they think?

30:49.325 --> 30:51.457
[overlapping chatter]

30:51.458 --> 30:53.155
♪ ♪

31:04.210 --> 31:06.428
- That's everybody.
- MOMMY: Thank God.

31:06.429 --> 31:08.387
Are you okay?

31:08.388 --> 31:11.694
Are you sure you're not gonna
call the cops, Russ? Come on.

31:11.695 --> 31:14.175
Frank, wh-what do you think
they're gonna do?

31:14.176 --> 31:15.698
Arrest it?

31:15.699 --> 31:16.961
So what are you guys-- Okay.

31:16.962 --> 31:18.224
What are you guys
gonna do tonight?

31:19.878 --> 31:21.226
I don't know.
We're gonna figure something...

31:21.227 --> 31:23.054
I'm not going back
in that house.

31:23.055 --> 31:24.794
You know what? Stop. You guys,
you're gonna stay with me.

31:24.795 --> 31:25.970
End of story.

31:25.971 --> 31:27.928
DADDO:
Okay, Frank, really,

31:27.929 --> 31:30.191
like, I-I haven't had
a chance to think.

31:30.192 --> 31:31.932
I don't-- We don't know
what this thing is.

31:31.933 --> 31:33.847
We don't even know
what's happening.

31:33.848 --> 31:35.457
I know, I know, I--
Which is more of a reason

31:35.458 --> 31:37.677
why you need to get your
fucking family out of here.

31:37.678 --> 31:39.070
- You have a kid, man.
- DADDO: I agree.

31:39.071 --> 31:41.333
I'm just thinking of
everybody here.

31:41.334 --> 31:42.595
[Daddo clears throat]

31:42.596 --> 31:46.164
Um... what about your mom?

31:46.165 --> 31:47.774
- Look, she's into this stuff...
- MOMMY: No, she's...

31:47.775 --> 31:49.645
She'd just say it was
fucking karma. I-- No, no.

31:49.646 --> 31:50.820
DADDO: Maybe she knows
experts or something.

31:50.821 --> 31:52.518
MOMMY:
We'll just go to a hotel.

31:52.519 --> 31:54.824
What are you gonna do,
live in a hotel? Seriously.

31:54.825 --> 31:58.002
[slow, raspy whispering]:
Bela.

31:58.003 --> 31:59.438
[conversation continues
indistinctly]

31:59.439 --> 32:02.572
[heavy, raspy breathing]

32:04.487 --> 32:06.358
UNCLE FRANK:
Come on, Daddo.

32:06.359 --> 32:08.360
What do you say, man?

32:08.361 --> 32:10.057
Let me take care of her.

32:10.058 --> 32:11.145
Okay.

32:11.146 --> 32:12.451
- Yeah?
- Okay.

32:12.452 --> 32:14.061
- All right.
- All right.

32:14.062 --> 32:16.759
Let's go to Uncle Frank's.

32:16.760 --> 32:20.633
DADDO:
<i>Type in, uh, "haunted house."</i>

32:20.634 --> 32:23.114
Or-or... or "ghost hunters."

32:23.115 --> 32:24.767
- "Demon hunters"?
- MOMMY: No, there's nothing.

32:24.768 --> 32:27.031
It's all podcasts.
It's bullshit.

32:27.032 --> 32:29.685
DADDO:
What about a priest?

32:29.686 --> 32:31.687
I actually grew up Catholic.

32:31.688 --> 32:33.080
- I know some priests.
- Wait!

32:33.081 --> 32:35.040
We forgot Vulchy.

32:38.130 --> 32:39.478
Um...

32:39.479 --> 32:41.088
Do you still have
your priest's number

32:41.089 --> 32:43.177
from when you were a kid?

32:43.178 --> 32:46.964
No, I did not have
my priest's number, thank God.

32:46.965 --> 32:48.967
♪ ♪

33:12.120 --> 33:14.208
DADDO:
Brave face, Bela.

33:14.209 --> 33:16.732
Okay?

33:16.733 --> 33:18.952
UNCLE FRANK:
Sleepover at Uncle Frank's.

33:18.953 --> 33:21.955
Are you sure you don't want
any of the guest bedrooms?

33:21.956 --> 33:24.392
Uh, where do you want
to sleep, Bela?

33:24.393 --> 33:26.307
I like it here.

33:26.308 --> 33:28.179
Is that okay
if we stay out here?

33:28.180 --> 33:29.746
UNCLE FRANK:
Yeah. Whatever's comfortable.

33:31.357 --> 33:32.835
Oh, check out
this couch over here.

33:32.836 --> 33:35.012
It doesn't fold out,
but it's way better than

33:35.013 --> 33:36.709
any mattress you've ever had
in your life.

33:36.710 --> 33:39.538
And that chair right there
massages.

33:39.539 --> 33:40.670
Sweet.

33:41.671 --> 33:43.237
There's two fridges.

33:43.238 --> 33:44.717
[security system beeping]

33:44.718 --> 33:46.762
[locks thumping]

33:46.763 --> 33:48.635
[melodic beep]

33:50.724 --> 33:53.117
What if it follows us?

33:53.118 --> 33:54.422
I don't think that's a thing.

33:54.423 --> 33:57.425
I think it's the house, right?

33:57.426 --> 33:58.948
Bela, what do you think?

33:58.949 --> 34:02.474
I mean, is it, is it here
right now?

34:02.475 --> 34:03.997
- I don't think so.
- DADDO: Okay.

34:03.998 --> 34:05.868
Well, if you see her,
tell her to go away,

34:05.869 --> 34:07.870
'cause Other Mommy
is not your friend.

34:07.871 --> 34:09.959
Stop.
Please stop calling it that.

34:09.960 --> 34:11.744
I'm sorry, but what do you...

34:11.745 --> 34:14.051
What is it exactly?

34:14.052 --> 34:15.791
- It's, like, uh...
- It w-- it was coming...

34:15.792 --> 34:17.793
It, like, pretends to be human,
but, uh, it's, like...

34:17.794 --> 34:19.404
Wow.

34:19.405 --> 34:22.494
And Bela says she takes her
to magical places.

34:22.495 --> 34:24.583
DADDO:
Yeah. "Special places"?

34:24.584 --> 34:26.324
What the fuck is that?

34:26.325 --> 34:28.327
♪ ♪

34:30.372 --> 34:31.851
DADDO:
It-It's fucking real, man.

34:31.852 --> 34:33.853
It is physical. It's...

34:33.854 --> 34:36.508
It was asking her
for carnations.

34:36.509 --> 34:38.727
- Yeah.
- Wow.

34:38.728 --> 34:40.642
And it looks like you.
Holy fuck.

34:40.643 --> 34:44.385
Should we be, like,
nailing crosses everywhere?

34:44.386 --> 34:46.779
It's-it's not funny.

34:46.780 --> 34:48.346
Hey, I'm sorry.

34:48.347 --> 34:51.132
Um, listen, the point is
you're safe here, okay?

34:52.786 --> 34:56.833
And, Russ, I think
you need to hang on to this.

34:58.357 --> 35:00.271
I don't want that around Bela.

35:00.272 --> 35:02.795
- [softly]: Hey.
- Why would you give that to us?

35:02.796 --> 35:04.753
DADDO: For real?
I'm gonna shoot the thing?

35:04.754 --> 35:06.015
UNCLE FRANK:
Listen, I don't even know

35:06.016 --> 35:07.539
if this thing is real,

35:07.540 --> 35:08.975
but this thing right here
will stop it, okay?

35:08.976 --> 35:11.108
- BELA: Mommy, look what I found.
- Trust me.

35:11.109 --> 35:14.459
Oh, wow. Great. Uh, yeah.

35:14.460 --> 35:16.287
That's, um, great work.

35:16.288 --> 35:18.941
You've got a good eye.

35:18.942 --> 35:21.119
How'd your sparkly case
get here?

35:22.337 --> 35:23.946
[stammers]

35:23.947 --> 35:25.123
[breath trembles]

35:28.038 --> 35:30.693
[thunder rumbling softly]

35:32.086 --> 35:34.132
[sighs]:
Okay.

35:36.046 --> 35:38.091
Come on.
It's past your bedtime.

35:38.092 --> 35:40.920
Let's go lie down.

35:40.921 --> 35:43.140
- Yeah, we're gonna read a story
and... -UNCLE FRANK: Yeah.

35:43.141 --> 35:44.880
Yeah, so, um,
you have everything here,

35:44.881 --> 35:47.231
and bathroom's downstairs.

35:47.232 --> 35:49.581
If you-- [stammers]
Just make yourself at home.

35:49.582 --> 35:52.453
<i>Mi casa es su casa,</i> so whatever
you guys need, all right?

35:52.454 --> 35:54.456
[slow heartbeat echoing]

36:04.597 --> 36:06.120
BELA [whispering]:
Daddo.

36:07.426 --> 36:08.991
Wake up.

36:08.992 --> 36:10.429
I need to pee.

36:11.691 --> 36:13.126
[Daddo snoring]

36:13.127 --> 36:15.173
[thunder rumbling softly]

36:35.367 --> 36:36.585
[sighs]

36:37.934 --> 36:39.371
Brave face.

36:45.377 --> 36:47.856
- [thunder rumbling softly]
- [rain pattering]

36:47.857 --> 36:49.685
[breath trembles]

37:00.783 --> 37:02.437
[thunder rumbling softly]

37:09.444 --> 37:11.837
♪ ♪

37:11.838 --> 37:13.840
[house creaking softly]

37:23.110 --> 37:25.155
[rain pattering]

37:29.899 --> 37:32.424
[panting]

37:57.623 --> 37:59.363
[soft creaking]

37:59.364 --> 38:01.366
♪ ♪

38:16.119 --> 38:17.337
[screams]

38:17.338 --> 38:19.297
[panting]

38:28.044 --> 38:30.090
♪ ♪

38:33.093 --> 38:35.137
[skin creaking]

38:35.138 --> 38:37.009
OTHER MOMMY [whispering]:
I didn't mean to scare you

38:37.010 --> 38:39.403
at the party.

38:39.404 --> 38:41.796
[whispering]: I'm not supposed
to talk to you anymore.

38:41.797 --> 38:43.537
[voice echoing]: You said
friends forgive each other

38:43.538 --> 38:44.799
no matter what.

38:44.800 --> 38:46.628
[whispering]:
They do, but...

38:51.285 --> 38:53.765
Aren't I your friend?

38:53.766 --> 38:56.202
[voice echoing]:
You are, but...

38:56.203 --> 38:58.596
me and Daddo are getting sadder.

38:58.597 --> 39:00.075
Things are worse now.

39:00.076 --> 39:02.774
[distorted echoing]:
Not because of me, Bela.

39:02.775 --> 39:04.471
Your parents are scared

39:04.472 --> 39:07.779
because they think
they know everything.

39:07.780 --> 39:09.824
But they don't.

39:09.825 --> 39:12.610
Daddo thinks
you're someone that died.

39:12.611 --> 39:14.613
- Is that true?
- No.

39:16.092 --> 39:18.660
I wasn't allowed to be a person.

39:21.620 --> 39:24.883
What if I did
something special for you?

39:24.884 --> 39:28.365
Something that made everyone
happy again.

39:28.366 --> 39:30.105
Like what?

39:30.106 --> 39:32.891
You already know.

39:32.892 --> 39:36.069
- What does your heart tell you?
- [heartbeat echoing]

39:37.984 --> 39:40.072
Sweet girl.

39:40.073 --> 39:42.422
Say it.

39:42.423 --> 39:45.599
Can you make Uncle Frank
go away?

39:45.600 --> 39:47.340
That's a great idea.

39:47.341 --> 39:49.124
[skin creaking]

39:49.125 --> 39:51.127
Wait, what are you gonna do?

39:52.520 --> 39:53.608
Other Mommy?

39:57.482 --> 39:58.961
[door closes]

40:00.136 --> 40:02.660
Oh. Hey, Bela.

40:02.661 --> 40:04.009
[door closes]

40:04.010 --> 40:06.925
Your parents still asleep?

40:06.926 --> 40:08.970
Oh, hey, honey, it's okay.

40:08.971 --> 40:11.320
Hey, it's okay. It's okay.

40:11.321 --> 40:13.540
- Hey, yeah.
- Leave me alone.

40:13.541 --> 40:16.414
No, no. Come on.

40:18.590 --> 40:20.505
Aren't we friends?

40:21.549 --> 40:23.550
You're trying to trick me.

40:23.551 --> 40:25.073
N-No, I-- No, I think

40:25.074 --> 40:27.119
if you feel like there's
something weird going on,

40:27.120 --> 40:29.121
- I'm just gonna call your dad.
- Mommy!

40:29.122 --> 40:30.296
What's wrong?

40:30.297 --> 40:31.645
I don't think it's Uncle Frank!

40:31.646 --> 40:33.299
No, don't! Mom, it's not safe!

40:33.300 --> 40:34.780
Bela had a little accident,
so...

40:39.262 --> 40:40.786
[muffled grunt]

40:43.789 --> 40:44.790
[sharp thud]

40:45.791 --> 40:47.314
[panting]

40:50.926 --> 40:52.928
[objects clattering]

40:54.582 --> 40:57.671
- [raspy growling, shrieking]
- [gunshots]

40:57.672 --> 40:59.674
- [Uncle Frank screaming]
- [gunshots continue]

41:04.157 --> 41:06.159
- [Uncle Frank screaming]
- [gunshots continue]

41:10.206 --> 41:11.817
[screaming and gunshots stop]

41:14.994 --> 41:16.603
[screaming]

41:16.604 --> 41:18.127
[panting]

41:23.916 --> 41:27.832
[distorted]: I didn't want you
to see me like this.

41:27.833 --> 41:29.008
Honey, close your eyes.

41:30.226 --> 41:32.314
- DADDO: Bela!
- Daddo!

41:32.315 --> 41:33.794
- [heavy footsteps]
- Holy...

41:33.795 --> 41:35.143
[raspy groaning]

41:35.144 --> 41:37.015
Get behind me.

41:37.016 --> 41:39.060
[Uncle Frank shouts]

41:39.061 --> 41:41.019
[screams]

41:41.020 --> 41:43.456
- [gasps]
- [Uncle Frank screams, gasps]

41:43.457 --> 41:45.197
[groaning]

41:45.198 --> 41:48.157
- MOMMY: What's going on?
- [Uncle Frank screaming]

41:52.466 --> 41:53.771
Frank!

41:53.772 --> 41:55.687
- No! No! No!
- Get out of my way!

41:59.647 --> 42:01.996
- DADDO: No! Bela!
- [Mommy screaming]

42:01.997 --> 42:03.782
[crackling]

42:06.654 --> 42:09.177
[high-pitched tone ringing]

42:09.178 --> 42:10.702
- [Daddo grunts]
- [muffled explosion]

42:16.229 --> 42:18.231
- [audio muffled]
- [coughing]

42:24.542 --> 42:26.412
MOMMY:
Frank. [sobs]

42:26.413 --> 42:27.545
Frank!

42:28.546 --> 42:30.416
Run!

42:30.417 --> 42:31.896
- Run! Go!
- [heavy footsteps]

42:31.897 --> 42:33.201
- Go!
- [glass shatters]

42:33.202 --> 42:34.725
- [panting]
- [light bulbs popping]

42:34.726 --> 42:37.379
[raspy growling]

42:37.380 --> 42:40.034
OTHER MOMMY [distorted]:
Bela, what did I do wrong?

42:40.035 --> 42:41.166
[screams]

42:41.167 --> 42:42.776
[raspy shrieking]

42:42.777 --> 42:44.604
- [Daddo shouts indistinctly]
- [Mommy screams]

42:44.605 --> 42:46.564
DADDO: He didn't give us
the fucking code!

42:51.351 --> 42:52.786
[screams]

42:52.787 --> 42:54.266
- Go! Drive! -I'm going!
- [engine revving]

42:54.267 --> 42:55.572
- Where do we go?!
- Go!

42:55.573 --> 42:56.790
DADDO:
I'm going!

42:56.791 --> 42:58.052
I'm going as fast as I can!

42:58.053 --> 42:59.228
MOMMY:
[screams] Go!

43:02.710 --> 43:04.712
[Mommy crying softly]

43:08.629 --> 43:11.544
DADDO:
I don't think I can do this.

43:11.545 --> 43:14.069
If we call the police,
they're gonna think we did it.

43:15.157 --> 43:16.594
Or I did it.

43:17.812 --> 43:20.205
There's not even a fucking body.

43:20.206 --> 43:21.860
[Mommy continues crying softly]

43:24.558 --> 43:26.604
MOMMY:
I'm so sorry. [sniffles]

43:28.344 --> 43:29.868
DADDO:
For what?

43:33.567 --> 43:35.829
I don't want to lie
to you anymore.

43:35.830 --> 43:38.790
- Please. Frank, he w--
- Don't. Don't. Don't!

43:42.228 --> 43:44.273
[vehicle door opens]

43:46.449 --> 43:47.886
[vehicle door closes]

43:56.416 --> 43:58.418
I'm glad you got some sleep.

43:59.549 --> 44:01.029
You want to get
something to eat?

44:02.422 --> 44:03.771
Okay.

44:12.258 --> 44:13.520
[locks beep]

44:15.304 --> 44:17.655
Mommy, are you okay?

44:21.659 --> 44:23.661
[sniffling]:
Yeah.

44:26.315 --> 44:29.187
I just needed some quiet time.

44:29.188 --> 44:31.190
[kids clamoring
and screaming playfully]

44:35.107 --> 44:37.022
[slurps]

44:38.066 --> 44:40.068
[game beeping]

44:52.385 --> 44:54.473
Maybe we can outrun it.

44:54.474 --> 44:56.083
Make it find somebody else.

44:56.084 --> 44:57.781
It's not just gonna stop.

44:57.782 --> 44:59.826
I'm just saying, we don't even
know what it wants.

44:59.827 --> 45:01.741
Bela, what does
Other Mommy want?

45:01.742 --> 45:03.917
- I don't think it's appropriate
to ask Bela. -Just let me...

45:03.918 --> 45:05.919
Carnations. I told you.

45:05.920 --> 45:08.575
She wants to switch places
with me.

45:11.796 --> 45:13.666
Do you mean...

45:13.667 --> 45:15.407
reincarnation?

45:15.408 --> 45:17.017
No, carnation.

45:17.018 --> 45:19.150
She'll be me.

45:19.151 --> 45:21.282
Only for a little bit.

45:21.283 --> 45:23.328
- So she can fix our family.
- DADDO: Okay.

45:23.329 --> 45:25.547
- There's nothing wrong with our
family. -Never-never say yes.

45:25.548 --> 45:27.811
Okay? Never, ever say yes, Bela.

45:27.812 --> 45:29.160
You understand me?

45:29.161 --> 45:30.945
She's lying.

45:32.817 --> 45:34.818
We have to kill this thing.

45:34.819 --> 45:36.515
Oh, great. Yeah, let's do that.

45:36.516 --> 45:37.864
I mean, do we even know
if that's possible?

45:37.865 --> 45:39.431
I don't know.
I don't know, Russ.

45:39.432 --> 45:41.041
She's trying to take
our daughter.

45:41.042 --> 45:42.651
Can you fight? Help me?

45:42.652 --> 45:44.437
Yes. Jesus.

45:46.134 --> 45:48.309
Okay.

45:48.310 --> 45:50.573
Well, you know
who we should ask.

45:51.618 --> 45:53.010
No.

45:53.011 --> 45:54.576
DADDO:
She hired that medium, right?

45:54.577 --> 45:56.361
- After your dad died.
- MOMMY: Oh, the scammers?

45:56.362 --> 45:57.884
- No.
- Maybe they're professionals.

45:57.885 --> 45:59.886
I mean, this is
what they do for a living.

45:59.887 --> 46:01.453
I mean, this is real.

46:01.454 --> 46:03.150
Like, what are we gonna do,
go to a church?

46:03.151 --> 46:05.196
- We can go anywhere but there.
- They'll c--

46:05.197 --> 46:07.241
- They'll call a social worker.
- Anywhere but my mom's.

46:07.242 --> 46:09.983
- I want to see Grandma.
- Yeah, I do, too.

46:09.984 --> 46:13.726
Yeah. Your m-mom doesn't think
it's a good idea, so...

46:13.727 --> 46:16.425
You should hear what she has
to say about you, Daddo.

46:18.906 --> 46:21.430
Well, this is not about that.

46:25.565 --> 46:27.000
Right, sorry.

46:27.001 --> 46:29.134
[ringtone playing]

46:30.178 --> 46:31.614
Hey, Lindsay.

46:32.659 --> 46:34.616
Oh, yeah,
I'm not coming in today.

46:34.617 --> 46:37.010
It's, um...

46:37.011 --> 46:38.490
[muffled]:
family emergency.

46:38.491 --> 46:41.885
[heavy footsteps running]

46:41.886 --> 46:44.104
- [light footsteps]
- [girl laughing]

46:44.105 --> 46:47.021
[kids chattering playfully,
laughing]

46:55.813 --> 46:58.249
This doesn't...

46:58.250 --> 46:59.598
actually happen to people.

46:59.599 --> 47:01.252
You understand that, right?

47:01.253 --> 47:04.081
I don't know if it's easier
being a kid, but...

47:04.082 --> 47:06.171
this is really hard.

47:11.959 --> 47:13.004
[softly]:
Hi.

47:16.007 --> 47:18.487
Is Uncle Frank dead?

47:21.882 --> 47:23.231
I don't know.

47:24.667 --> 47:27.147
I think so.

47:27.148 --> 47:29.889
I didn't mean
for that to happen.

47:29.890 --> 47:32.762
Just wanted Mommy
to love you again.

47:41.423 --> 47:43.121
She does.

47:44.862 --> 47:47.428
She loved Uncle Frank, too.

47:47.429 --> 47:49.039
I know.

47:49.040 --> 47:50.258
[sighs]

47:52.391 --> 47:55.262
Sometimes grown-ups, they, um...

47:55.263 --> 47:56.960
they fall in love
with other people

47:56.961 --> 48:00.180
even though they shouldn't.

48:00.181 --> 48:03.881
But... Mom's always
gonna love us.

48:08.320 --> 48:09.842
We're gonna be fine.

48:09.843 --> 48:11.278
- [kids screaming playfully]
- GIRL: Sorry.

48:11.279 --> 48:13.020
- DADDO: Jesus.
- [kids laughing]

48:18.156 --> 48:19.547
[chuckles]

48:19.548 --> 48:20.810
Mm-mm.

48:22.029 --> 48:23.378
I'm sorry.

48:24.379 --> 48:25.727
[Bela murmurs]

48:25.728 --> 48:27.860
[sighs] Okay. Okay.

48:27.861 --> 48:31.081
You can go, you can go right up
there to where I can see you.

48:31.082 --> 48:32.430
- BELA: Thanks, Daddo.
- All right? Be careful.

48:32.431 --> 48:34.912
[girl laughing]

48:40.874 --> 48:43.832
GIRL [voice echoing]:
Hey, you want to play termites?

48:43.833 --> 48:46.226
BELA:
How do you play?

48:46.227 --> 48:48.098
You're the bug,
and I try to squish you.

48:48.099 --> 48:49.838
Wait.

48:49.839 --> 48:52.015
I've got to go ask
my Daddo first.

48:52.016 --> 48:54.018
♪ ♪

48:57.717 --> 48:59.719
- [compass rattling]
- [kids chattering playfully]

49:01.721 --> 49:04.070
[kids screaming playfully,
laughing]

49:04.071 --> 49:05.724
Okay, Bela. It's time to go.

49:05.725 --> 49:06.944
Come on down.

49:08.075 --> 49:10.251
Yeah. I see you.

49:11.644 --> 49:13.646
[rattling]

49:18.216 --> 49:19.433
Bela?

49:19.434 --> 49:20.913
- [rapid thumping]
- [girl laughing]

49:20.914 --> 49:22.480
Daddo?

49:22.481 --> 49:24.526
♪ ♪

49:30.228 --> 49:31.664
Daddo?

49:32.839 --> 49:34.232
[girl laughs]

49:43.415 --> 49:44.763
- [girl screams]
- [gasps]

49:44.764 --> 49:46.112
OTHER MOMMY [distorted]:
I've got you.

49:46.113 --> 49:47.809
Little bug, little bug,
little bug.

49:47.810 --> 49:48.897
[rapid thumping]

49:48.898 --> 49:51.509
Oh, what's the matter, Bela?

49:51.510 --> 49:53.946
Aren't you happy
I made Uncle Frank go away?

49:53.947 --> 49:56.340
No! I didn't ask for that!

49:56.341 --> 49:58.777
Yes, you did.

49:58.778 --> 50:01.520
I made him sparkle for you.

50:02.912 --> 50:05.262
BELA:
They're gonna know I'm gone!

50:05.263 --> 50:07.613
OTHER MOMMY:
<i>No, they won't. [chuckles]</i>

50:11.182 --> 50:12.312
[gasps]

50:12.313 --> 50:13.966
OTHER MOMMY:
I'm sorry, Bela.

50:13.967 --> 50:15.489
- Bela, can't we be friends?
- No! Leave me alone!

50:15.490 --> 50:18.275
Come on, Bela,
let's play silly faces.

50:18.276 --> 50:20.668
I'll be you and you'll be me.

50:20.669 --> 50:22.235
It'll be fun.

50:22.236 --> 50:24.238
Let me be human.

50:26.240 --> 50:28.285
- [kids screaming playfully]
- [heavy thump]

50:28.286 --> 50:30.113
[Bela grunting]

50:30.114 --> 50:31.418
[playful chatter]

50:31.419 --> 50:32.985
Bela!

50:32.986 --> 50:34.073
[grunts]

50:34.074 --> 50:36.380
[panting]

50:36.381 --> 50:38.382
- I got you.
- Ow!

50:38.383 --> 50:40.385
- [raspy shrieking]
- [Bela screaming]

50:42.517 --> 50:43.909
No, I don't want that, Lindsay.

50:43.910 --> 50:45.824
I just-- I have to be here.

50:45.825 --> 50:48.261
[concerned chatter]

50:48.262 --> 50:49.828
- Oh, a few days.
- MAN: Did you see that?

50:49.829 --> 50:52.222
- MAN 2: Is she all right?
- WOMAN: What happened?

50:52.223 --> 50:53.615
Actually, you know what?
I don't give a fuck.

50:54.616 --> 50:57.966
Bela! Bela!

50:57.967 --> 50:59.185
Bela!

50:59.186 --> 51:01.536
[balls rumbling]

51:03.582 --> 51:05.366
[screams, grunts]

51:06.367 --> 51:08.194
- [screams]
- Bela!

51:08.195 --> 51:09.978
- Bela! Bela!
- [screaming]

51:09.979 --> 51:11.937
[grunting]

51:11.938 --> 51:13.243
- Bela!
- [screaming continues]

51:13.244 --> 51:14.722
[concerned chatter]

51:14.723 --> 51:16.594
MOMMY:
Excuse me.

51:16.595 --> 51:17.725
DADDO:
Bela!

51:17.726 --> 51:18.944
Where is she?!

51:18.945 --> 51:20.293
DADDO:
It took her down!

51:20.294 --> 51:21.773
Come on, help me!

51:21.774 --> 51:22.862
Help me!

51:23.863 --> 51:25.472
- [grunts]
- Oh, God.

51:25.473 --> 51:26.604
- Where is she?!
- They're under here somewhere!

51:26.605 --> 51:28.520
MOMMY:
[grunts] Bela!

51:30.174 --> 51:31.304
Bela!

51:31.305 --> 51:33.132
[balls rumbling]

51:33.133 --> 51:35.135
[Bela screaming]

51:38.573 --> 51:40.705
OTHER MOMMY [distorted]:
Where should we go, Bela?

51:40.706 --> 51:42.924
Anywhere you want.

51:42.925 --> 51:45.145
I want to go home!

51:46.407 --> 51:47.668
[grunts]

51:47.669 --> 51:49.715
[panting]

51:51.847 --> 51:53.893
[faint, rapid heartbeat]

51:57.418 --> 51:59.420
♪ ♪

52:10.170 --> 52:12.172
[heartbeat fades]

52:18.222 --> 52:20.005
- Bela!
- [screaming]

52:20.006 --> 52:22.094
- Should we see the ocean?
- [water splashes]

52:22.095 --> 52:24.141
[water burbling]

52:29.015 --> 52:30.364
[gasping]

52:39.939 --> 52:42.636
Please! Take me back!

52:42.637 --> 52:44.682
Take me back!

52:44.683 --> 52:46.640
[car alarms honking and wailing]

52:46.641 --> 52:48.555
♪ ♪

52:48.556 --> 52:51.036
Take me back, Other Mommy!

52:51.037 --> 52:54.257
♪ ♪

52:54.258 --> 52:56.216
[car alarms continue
honking and wailing]

52:59.437 --> 53:02.308
OTHER MOMMY [whispers]:
If you say so.

53:02.309 --> 53:04.050
[loud rumbling]

53:07.880 --> 53:09.882
[car alarms continue
honking and wailing]

53:13.929 --> 53:15.321
[gasps]

53:15.322 --> 53:16.931
- Excuse us. Sorry.
- Excuse me. Sorry.

53:16.932 --> 53:18.585
[car alarms honking
and wailing outside]

53:18.586 --> 53:20.370
Bela.

53:20.371 --> 53:22.373
[car alarms continue
honking and wailing]

53:24.592 --> 53:26.594
- [balls rumbling]
- [water burbling]

53:35.299 --> 53:37.822
[breath trembles]

53:37.823 --> 53:39.476
Bela!

53:39.477 --> 53:43.872
[singsongy]: Your parents
are lying to you, Bela.

53:46.223 --> 53:50.443
[whispering]:
She wishes you never existed.

53:50.444 --> 53:51.532
[creaking]

53:53.360 --> 53:54.621
[car alarms continue
honking and wailing]

53:54.622 --> 53:56.493
[gasping, coughing]

53:56.494 --> 53:58.496
MOMMY:
Bela! Honey.

53:59.671 --> 54:01.933
- Mommy.
- Bela. Honey.

54:01.934 --> 54:03.979
- Oh, my God. [panting]
- [coughing, sobbing]

54:07.026 --> 54:08.592
BELA:
Come here, Daddo.

54:08.593 --> 54:10.202
[concerned chatter]

54:10.203 --> 54:11.857
WOMAN:
I have no idea.

54:12.858 --> 54:13.989
[exhales]

54:17.471 --> 54:18.558
[exhales]

54:18.559 --> 54:20.561
♪ ♪

54:30.528 --> 54:32.050
[distorted screams]

54:32.051 --> 54:33.705
[intercom buzzes]

54:36.185 --> 54:39.231
Hey, Mom, it's us. We're here.

54:39.232 --> 54:41.886
GRANDMA RUTH:
Drive up and remove your socks.

54:41.887 --> 54:43.931
See? I told you,
she's lost her mind.

54:43.932 --> 54:45.890
She's probably peeing
in milk bottles up there.

54:45.891 --> 54:47.065
- [Daddo chuckles]
- Ew.

54:47.066 --> 54:49.197
DADDO:
Mmm. Sounds yummy.

54:49.198 --> 54:50.983
[gates creaking]

54:53.246 --> 54:55.639
GRANDMA RUTH:
It's safe to come out now.

54:55.640 --> 54:58.294
[seagulls squawking]

54:58.295 --> 54:59.643
[dogs barking]

54:59.644 --> 55:00.861
I needed your socks
for the dogs.

55:00.862 --> 55:02.472
Hi!

55:02.473 --> 55:03.734
GRANDMA RUTH:
They have to accept your scent

55:03.735 --> 55:05.039
- before you can come in.
- [Bela laughing]

55:05.040 --> 55:06.824
DADDO:
Guard dogs, Ruth?

55:06.825 --> 55:09.305
MOMMY: Yeah, the crystals
aren't doing the trick anymore?

55:09.306 --> 55:12.220
I prefer a little more bite.

55:12.221 --> 55:13.396
- They're so pretty.
- [dogs panting]

55:13.397 --> 55:14.484
[chuckles]

55:14.485 --> 55:16.921
This house is protected.

55:16.922 --> 55:20.011
My "scammer" friends
are coming tomorrow.

55:20.012 --> 55:21.752
They'll fix your problem.

55:21.753 --> 55:23.276
[vehicle locks beep]

55:24.582 --> 55:26.497
You guys look like
you could use a drink.

55:28.020 --> 55:29.064
[door closes]

55:31.893 --> 55:34.417
I meant to ask, how's Dad doing?

55:34.418 --> 55:37.245
You two talk pretty regularly,
I heard.

55:37.246 --> 55:39.945
GRANDMA RUTH:
As a matter of fact, we do.

55:41.860 --> 55:44.775
He was the love of my life.

55:44.776 --> 55:48.213
Which is hard to find,
as you know.

55:48.214 --> 55:49.736
Fantastic. Not upsetting at all.

55:49.737 --> 55:51.173
Tell him I said hi.

55:52.174 --> 55:53.959
He asks about you.

55:56.309 --> 55:57.658
He asking about me, too?

55:58.616 --> 56:00.139
[chuckles]

56:02.184 --> 56:03.882
Hardly.

56:10.976 --> 56:13.195
Is that where you keep
your milk bottles, Grandma?

56:14.196 --> 56:15.458
What's that, honey?

56:15.459 --> 56:17.373
For your pee?

56:17.374 --> 56:19.854
[Mommy and Daddo laughing]

56:22.030 --> 56:24.032
- [waves crashing]
- [dogs barking]

56:26.165 --> 56:28.166
[panting]

56:28.167 --> 56:30.212
♪ ♪

56:31.997 --> 56:34.739
[barking]

56:37.481 --> 56:40.526
[wind whistling]

56:40.527 --> 56:44.225
GRANDMA RUTH: Your mother and I
used to sit down here and talk.

56:44.226 --> 56:46.577
Back when we talked at all.
[chuckles]

56:49.971 --> 56:52.495
People like to say
you can't choose your family.

56:52.496 --> 56:55.323
You're stuck with them for life.

56:55.324 --> 56:58.805
You get older, you realize
that's not exactly true.

56:58.806 --> 57:00.285
[chuckles]

57:00.286 --> 57:03.157
No one's love is guaranteed.

57:03.158 --> 57:05.769
It's always a choice.

57:05.770 --> 57:07.988
You're not supposed to lie
to the people you love.

57:07.989 --> 57:10.251
[laughs]

57:10.252 --> 57:12.820
Yeah, but we all do.

57:14.605 --> 57:17.868
People you love
are going to lie to you,

57:17.869 --> 57:21.263
just like people who hurt you
are gonna say they love you.

57:22.656 --> 57:24.962
Other Mommy said

57:24.963 --> 57:28.226
she can make it
so I won't ever get hurt.

57:28.227 --> 57:32.448
Oh, that's the biggest lie
of all, isn't it?

57:32.449 --> 57:34.058
What do you mean?

57:34.059 --> 57:37.583
Nobody gets through life
without a few scars, Bela.

57:37.584 --> 57:40.195
That's what makes us powerful.

57:41.153 --> 57:43.198
That's being human.

57:45.244 --> 57:47.027
It's...

57:47.028 --> 57:49.161
scary and it's beautiful.

57:50.336 --> 57:51.772
And it hurts.

57:52.817 --> 57:54.862
But we're lucky to do it.

57:55.907 --> 57:58.082
Don't ever forget that.

57:58.083 --> 58:00.128
♪ ♪

58:11.183 --> 58:15.142
I have some very powerful
friends coming tomorrow.

58:15.143 --> 58:18.016
They're not afraid
of Other Mommy.

58:19.060 --> 58:21.322
<i>She'll be afraid of them.</i>

58:21.323 --> 58:23.369
[vehicles approaching]

58:24.544 --> 58:26.546
[horns honking in distance]

58:28.896 --> 58:31.942
Uh-oh. Cavalry's coming.

58:31.943 --> 58:33.378
Want to see?

58:33.379 --> 58:36.773
- [engines revving]
- [tires screeching]

58:36.774 --> 58:39.645
- [busy chatter]
- BRIAN: Where are my monitors?

58:39.646 --> 58:41.386
MAN:
All right, 10-4. I'm on it.

58:41.387 --> 58:42.735
BRIAN:
Be careful with those.

58:42.736 --> 58:44.345
- [dog barks]
- [chatter continues]

58:44.346 --> 58:45.999
LOIS: Well, it's nice
to see you again, Ruth.

58:46.000 --> 58:48.307
Considering the circumstances.

58:49.656 --> 58:50.830
- Hello.
- Hi.

58:50.831 --> 58:52.266
I'm Lois Anthony.

58:52.267 --> 58:53.920
I'm grateful to be here.

58:53.921 --> 58:56.357
Yeah, well,
we're-we're grateful.

58:56.358 --> 58:57.707
Really.

58:57.708 --> 58:59.360
LOIS:
I've helped a lot of people

58:59.361 --> 59:01.667
- in situations like yours.
- [computers beeping]

59:01.668 --> 59:03.364
There's nothing to be afraid of.

59:03.365 --> 59:05.845
GRANDMA RUTH: Lois guided me
when we lost Grandpa.

59:05.846 --> 59:08.892
When she tells spirits
what to do, they listen.

59:08.893 --> 59:12.156
BRIAN:
Keep bringing those in, please.

59:12.157 --> 59:14.854
Poltergeists can throw objects
up to 100 miles an hour.

59:14.855 --> 59:16.074
[bag thuds]

59:17.292 --> 59:19.685
What kind of a entity or...

59:19.686 --> 59:21.861
wh-what-what do you think it is?

59:21.862 --> 59:23.210
LOIS:
It's a trickster.

59:23.211 --> 59:24.777
A corrupted energy
seeking a host,

59:24.778 --> 59:26.823
intruding from another plane.

59:26.824 --> 59:28.694
Cool. Okay.

59:28.695 --> 59:30.566
BRIAN:
Keep this bracelet on.

59:30.567 --> 59:34.439
It's gonna tell me how your
body's reacting on the inside.

59:34.440 --> 59:37.355
- Like my heart?
- Yeah, exactly.

59:37.356 --> 59:40.837
You'll be able to see
if something goes inside of it?

59:40.838 --> 59:42.316
Inside your heart?

59:42.317 --> 59:44.710
It's probably nothing you did.

59:44.711 --> 59:47.452
These monsters are always
drawn to children

59:47.453 --> 59:49.019
because of their innocence.

59:49.020 --> 59:50.934
They slip through the cracks
into our world,

59:50.935 --> 59:53.719
but they need permission
to exist.

59:53.720 --> 59:55.895
As soon as Bela's innocence
is broken,

59:55.896 --> 59:57.288
the demon won't
want her anymore.

59:57.289 --> 59:58.768
So are you saying

59:58.769 --> 01:00:00.378
we're supposed to make her
less innocent?

01:00:00.379 --> 01:00:02.641
No, no.

01:00:02.642 --> 01:00:04.731
We're here to kill the monster.

01:00:16.438 --> 01:00:19.658
[typing on keyboard]

01:00:19.659 --> 01:00:24.316
We light this candle to
ward off those that fear fire.

01:00:28.276 --> 01:00:33.454
We pour this cup to ward off
those that fear water.

01:00:33.455 --> 01:00:35.066
Hmm.

01:00:36.981 --> 01:00:38.417
We spill this salt...

01:00:42.421 --> 01:00:45.642
...to ward off those
that fear the earth.

01:00:47.426 --> 01:00:49.036
[bell rings]

01:01:05.444 --> 01:01:06.705
- [sneezes]
- [gasps]

01:01:06.706 --> 01:01:08.752
Fucking dogs.

01:01:10.754 --> 01:01:14.627
We wish to be heard by the
entity known as Other Mommy.

01:01:16.847 --> 01:01:18.935
No more hiding.

01:01:18.936 --> 01:01:20.633
It's time for you to go.

01:01:22.156 --> 01:01:25.463
We're not afraid of you,
Other Mommy.

01:01:25.464 --> 01:01:27.640
Your fun is over.

01:01:29.120 --> 01:01:30.295
[mouse clicking]

01:01:33.167 --> 01:01:34.385
[heavy thumping upstairs]

01:01:34.386 --> 01:01:36.343
[gasping]

01:01:36.344 --> 01:01:38.564
[dogs growl, whimper]

01:01:39.565 --> 01:01:41.393
Caught that. Upstairs.

01:01:42.350 --> 01:01:44.264
You don't belong here!

01:01:44.265 --> 01:01:45.352
- [house creaking]
- Mommy.

01:01:45.353 --> 01:01:47.441
- It's okay.
- [panting]

01:01:47.442 --> 01:01:49.313
- [shushing]
- This girl is

01:01:49.314 --> 01:01:51.141
under my protection.

01:01:51.142 --> 01:01:52.926
We have the power here.

01:01:54.014 --> 01:01:56.581
This is Bela's life, not yours.

01:01:56.582 --> 01:01:58.888
[beeping steadily]

01:01:58.889 --> 01:02:01.238
- [loud bang, rumbling]
- [gasping]

01:02:01.239 --> 01:02:03.327
[cameras clicking]

01:02:03.328 --> 01:02:05.329
- Wow.
- [computer beeping steadily]

01:02:05.330 --> 01:02:06.852
Wow, okay.

01:02:06.853 --> 01:02:08.245
Motion sensors, zone four,
upstairs hall.

01:02:08.246 --> 01:02:09.681
What does that mean?

01:02:09.682 --> 01:02:12.162
- [loud bang]
- [cameras clicking]

01:02:12.163 --> 01:02:13.641
BRIAN:
Oh, fuck. Zone two.

01:02:13.642 --> 01:02:16.557
Downstairs now? How the fuck?

01:02:16.558 --> 01:02:18.951
LOIS: We ask
that you move on from Bela.

01:02:18.952 --> 01:02:21.954
She's tired.
Her family is tired.

01:02:21.955 --> 01:02:23.870
- [cameras clicking]
- [raspy whooshing]

01:02:27.482 --> 01:02:30.658
[thunder rumbling softly]

01:02:30.659 --> 01:02:32.966
- [steady beeping]
- Do you see it, Brian?

01:02:34.011 --> 01:02:35.707
No, still nothing.

01:02:35.708 --> 01:02:37.753
[footsteps upstairs]

01:02:37.754 --> 01:02:39.756
[cameras clicking]

01:02:44.151 --> 01:02:46.153
♪ ♪

01:02:50.810 --> 01:02:52.812
[deep whooshing]

01:02:54.335 --> 01:02:56.293
- [table rattling]
- [bell ringing]

01:02:56.294 --> 01:02:57.555
[gasping]

01:02:57.556 --> 01:02:59.078
Guys, it's gonna be all right!

01:02:59.079 --> 01:03:00.123
[mouthing]

01:03:00.124 --> 01:03:02.039
I illuminate you!

01:03:03.736 --> 01:03:06.172
We demand that you show
yourself to us, Other Mommy!

01:03:06.173 --> 01:03:07.608
Wait, what?!

01:03:07.609 --> 01:03:09.175
Show yourself!

01:03:09.176 --> 01:03:10.874
[rumbling]

01:03:15.574 --> 01:03:16.835
I want to leave.

01:03:16.836 --> 01:03:18.619
DADDO:
Brave faces.

01:03:18.620 --> 01:03:20.927
Brave faces, okay?
This is why we came here.

01:03:22.581 --> 01:03:24.583
- BRIAN: Wait. Wait.
- [rumbling fades]

01:03:26.150 --> 01:03:27.541
I think...

01:03:27.542 --> 01:03:29.021
[static over headphones]

01:03:29.022 --> 01:03:30.414
Whispering.

01:03:30.415 --> 01:03:32.417
- [panting]
- [eerie voices whispering]

01:03:37.335 --> 01:03:38.988
What do you see, honey?

01:03:38.989 --> 01:03:40.685
[raspy shrieking]

01:03:40.686 --> 01:03:42.426
Zone one! Right here!
It's in here!

01:03:42.427 --> 01:03:44.036
Switching to UV.

01:03:44.037 --> 01:03:46.299
[lights clicking, whirring]

01:03:46.300 --> 01:03:47.823
LOIS:
Go check for footprints.

01:03:47.824 --> 01:03:49.302
Everything's okay.

01:03:49.303 --> 01:03:51.130
We have Other Mommy
right where we want her.

01:03:51.131 --> 01:03:52.958
Oh, here.

01:03:52.959 --> 01:03:54.220
Get out of here.
Get out of here.

01:03:54.221 --> 01:03:55.656
Get out-- Get out of here.

01:03:55.657 --> 01:03:56.788
Get out of here.

01:03:56.789 --> 01:03:58.268
[sneezes]

01:03:58.269 --> 01:04:00.009
Fuck!

01:04:00.010 --> 01:04:01.750
- [gasps]
- She's here!

01:04:03.013 --> 01:04:04.623
- Other Mommy!
- DADDO: No.

01:04:05.624 --> 01:04:07.712
[raspy breathing]

01:04:07.713 --> 01:04:09.540
LOIS:
Oh, my God.

01:04:09.541 --> 01:04:11.324
It's the mom.

01:04:11.325 --> 01:04:12.848
Get rid of it!

01:04:12.849 --> 01:04:14.676
[shivering]:
No.

01:04:17.027 --> 01:04:18.418
[chuckles]

01:04:18.419 --> 01:04:20.899
- We did it!
- [dogs barking]

01:04:20.900 --> 01:04:23.293
BRIAN: Our first fucking ghost!
It's real!

01:04:23.294 --> 01:04:25.208
- I told you. I told you.
- It's fucking real!

01:04:25.209 --> 01:04:26.731
You fucks! You fakes!

01:04:26.732 --> 01:04:27.819
Hey, come on.

01:04:27.820 --> 01:04:29.516
Let's go, let's go!

01:04:29.517 --> 01:04:30.909
[exhales softly]

01:04:30.910 --> 01:04:31.911
[grunts]

01:04:33.434 --> 01:04:34.479
[grunts]

01:04:35.784 --> 01:04:37.176
BRIAN [over comms]:
Lois.

01:04:37.177 --> 01:04:38.744
Lois.

01:04:41.399 --> 01:04:42.922
[gasping]

01:04:45.142 --> 01:04:46.273
[distorted bark]

01:04:49.189 --> 01:04:50.711
[distorted bark]

01:04:50.712 --> 01:04:52.975
[Lois gasping]

01:04:52.976 --> 01:04:55.065
[Lois whimpering]

01:04:57.110 --> 01:04:59.372
[screaming]

01:04:59.373 --> 01:05:01.461
[distorted yelling]

01:05:01.462 --> 01:05:03.289
[cameras clicking]

01:05:03.290 --> 01:05:04.464
[growling]

01:05:04.465 --> 01:05:06.858
- [screaming]
- BRIAN: Lois!

01:05:06.859 --> 01:05:08.774
[screaming continues]

01:05:12.778 --> 01:05:14.518
[screaming]

01:05:14.519 --> 01:05:16.216
- [wheezes]
- [grunts]

01:05:18.740 --> 01:05:20.132
[Other Mommy roaring]

01:05:20.133 --> 01:05:21.221
[yelling]

01:05:24.050 --> 01:05:25.878
[screaming]

01:05:29.882 --> 01:05:31.491
Come on! Go, go, go!

01:05:31.492 --> 01:05:33.538
♪ ♪

01:05:43.069 --> 01:05:44.462
[bracelet beeping rapidly]

01:05:50.511 --> 01:05:52.295
OTHER MOMMY: Did you think
you could get rid of me?

01:05:52.296 --> 01:05:53.600
[screams]

01:05:53.601 --> 01:05:55.777
[panting]

01:05:56.996 --> 01:05:58.605
I tried being your friend.

01:05:58.606 --> 01:06:01.131
[crying]:
I'm sorry!

01:06:02.175 --> 01:06:04.089
- You've had your chance.
- [crying]

01:06:04.090 --> 01:06:06.091
[bracelet beeping faster]

01:06:06.092 --> 01:06:09.747
[distorted]:
But I'm done asking nicely.

01:06:09.748 --> 01:06:11.576
[dog whines]

01:06:12.533 --> 01:06:14.491
[whimpering]

01:06:14.492 --> 01:06:17.625
DADDO [in distance]:
Bela! Bela!

01:06:20.019 --> 01:06:21.498
- Here!
- DADDO: She's there?

01:06:21.499 --> 01:06:23.674
- She's down here!
- She's there!

01:06:23.675 --> 01:06:24.762
Bela!

01:06:24.763 --> 01:06:26.808
♪ ♪

01:06:29.159 --> 01:06:31.074
[thunder rumbling softly]

01:06:38.646 --> 01:06:40.692
♪ ♪

01:06:53.835 --> 01:06:55.185
[grunts]

01:06:56.316 --> 01:06:57.665
[sighs]

01:07:03.715 --> 01:07:05.760
I don't know where to go.

01:07:09.460 --> 01:07:10.852
Well...

01:07:12.376 --> 01:07:14.943
...we can't keep bringing
other people into this.

01:07:20.340 --> 01:07:22.342
Sh-Should we just go home?

01:07:27.130 --> 01:07:28.478
Yeah.

01:07:28.479 --> 01:07:30.568
- May as well be comfortable.
- Okay.

01:07:33.614 --> 01:07:36.269
We still got that cookie dough
in the freezer, right?

01:07:40.186 --> 01:07:41.709
Okay.

01:08:06.647 --> 01:08:08.518
MOMMY:
We'll be fine, honey.

01:08:08.519 --> 01:08:09.955
Come here.

01:08:16.092 --> 01:08:17.310
[vehicle door closes]

01:08:43.336 --> 01:08:45.338
- Oh, God.
- [gasps]

01:08:47.253 --> 01:08:49.907
We left the lights on.

01:08:49.908 --> 01:08:51.430
Are you kidding me?

01:08:51.431 --> 01:08:53.738
- [rumbling]
- [bubbles sizzling]

01:09:05.532 --> 01:09:07.317
[glass squeaking]

01:09:17.892 --> 01:09:19.155
Bela?

01:09:22.680 --> 01:09:24.942
Tonight...

01:09:24.943 --> 01:09:28.641
I think, in order
to get through this,

01:09:28.642 --> 01:09:31.731
we all need to be someone else.

01:09:31.732 --> 01:09:33.560
What do you mean?

01:09:35.475 --> 01:09:37.869
We're done running.
This is our home.

01:09:44.310 --> 01:09:46.704
I think we should
dress up tonight.

01:09:48.401 --> 01:09:50.011
Have a little party?

01:09:51.099 --> 01:09:53.884
Can I wear some of your jewelry?

01:09:53.885 --> 01:09:55.842
You can wear all of my jewelry.

01:09:55.843 --> 01:09:57.322
[boops]

01:09:57.323 --> 01:09:59.759
[ice rattling]

01:09:59.760 --> 01:10:01.587
DADDO:
Just...

01:10:01.588 --> 01:10:03.633
like that.

01:10:03.634 --> 01:10:05.069
- [chuckles]
- Okay.

01:10:05.070 --> 01:10:06.940
[whispering]:
Bring this to Mommy.

01:10:06.941 --> 01:10:08.986
Surprise her and tell her she
can put the broom down, okay?

01:10:08.987 --> 01:10:10.770
- Okay.
- Okay.

01:10:10.771 --> 01:10:13.120
Can I try it?

01:10:13.121 --> 01:10:14.732
Go for it.

01:10:16.560 --> 01:10:18.952
- I like it.
- [laughs]: Okay.

01:10:18.953 --> 01:10:22.956
♪ I got your name
on a matchbook... ♪

01:10:22.957 --> 01:10:26.090
Daddo says
to put the broom down.

01:10:26.091 --> 01:10:28.223
Happy to.

01:10:28.224 --> 01:10:29.834
- Ah, cheers.
- Cheers.

01:10:30.835 --> 01:10:31.966
Mm.

01:10:32.967 --> 01:10:34.838
Think we have enough?

01:10:34.839 --> 01:10:36.231
Yeah.

01:10:36.232 --> 01:10:38.103
I bet she's shaking
in her boots.

01:10:40.061 --> 01:10:42.107
Well, this is everything we got.

01:10:43.500 --> 01:10:45.241
[sighs]

01:10:47.417 --> 01:10:48.678
What do you think?

01:10:48.679 --> 01:10:50.201
Does Mom look like a badass?

01:10:50.202 --> 01:10:51.289
DADDO:
I think you do.

01:10:51.290 --> 01:10:53.683
[Bela and Daddo chuckling]

01:10:53.684 --> 01:10:55.772
I am, uh,
trying to choose between

01:10:55.773 --> 01:10:58.471
the crowbar and...

01:11:00.473 --> 01:11:02.561
...cleaver? I don't know.

01:11:02.562 --> 01:11:03.781
[Mommy and Daddo laugh]

01:11:05.870 --> 01:11:08.873
["Favourite Shirts [Boy Meets
Girl]" by Haircut 100 playing]

01:11:10.266 --> 01:11:11.440
You hear that?

01:11:11.441 --> 01:11:13.746
You know this song.

01:11:13.747 --> 01:11:15.880
Wait a second. Is he gonna...?

01:11:17.795 --> 01:11:19.491
At a time like this?

01:11:19.492 --> 01:11:22.494
How could he? How dare he?

01:11:22.495 --> 01:11:24.061
♪ Time can't afford no time... ♪

01:11:24.062 --> 01:11:25.541
- Oh, no.
- [chuckles] Crazy.

01:11:25.542 --> 01:11:27.673
- Turn the volume up!
- [music volume increases]

01:11:27.674 --> 01:11:28.848
♪ Someday maybe ♪

01:11:28.849 --> 01:11:31.111
♪ Boy meets girl... ♪

01:11:31.112 --> 01:11:32.852
[grunts] Come on, Bela.

01:11:32.853 --> 01:11:35.551
You want to dance with Daddo?

01:11:35.552 --> 01:11:38.031
♪ Boy meets girl... ♪

01:11:38.032 --> 01:11:39.338
Come on.

01:11:42.123 --> 01:11:43.863
BELA:
It's okay, Daddo.

01:11:43.864 --> 01:11:46.084
You guys can stop pretending.

01:11:49.740 --> 01:11:52.003
Yeah. Okay.

01:11:53.134 --> 01:11:54.483
Okay.

01:11:54.484 --> 01:11:55.746
[song stops]

01:11:56.703 --> 01:11:59.357
♪ ♪

01:11:59.358 --> 01:12:01.317
[clears throat]
Why don't you...

01:12:02.796 --> 01:12:04.711
...pick one you like?

01:12:09.107 --> 01:12:10.629
[picks up cleaver]

01:12:10.630 --> 01:12:12.284
- Your cleaver.
- Thank you.

01:12:23.774 --> 01:12:26.690
I'm actually really scared.

01:12:28.387 --> 01:12:29.822
[chuckles softly]

01:12:29.823 --> 01:12:31.956
I'm glad you said it.

01:12:35.612 --> 01:12:36.742
[inhales deeply]

01:12:36.743 --> 01:12:38.702
Same team. [chuckles softly]

01:12:39.877 --> 01:12:41.444
Always.

01:12:43.924 --> 01:12:45.316
[loud banging, rumbling]

01:12:45.317 --> 01:12:47.363
[raspy yelling]

01:12:48.668 --> 01:12:50.452
[raspy growling]

01:12:50.453 --> 01:12:51.454
[gasps]

01:12:53.543 --> 01:12:55.065
Bela, stay right...

01:12:55.066 --> 01:12:56.327
[Other Mommy roars]

01:12:56.328 --> 01:12:58.112
- Daddo!
- Get under!

01:12:59.070 --> 01:13:00.505
[whimpers]

01:13:00.506 --> 01:13:02.160
- [Daddo and Mommy grunting]
- [gasping]

01:13:04.380 --> 01:13:06.511
[screams]

01:13:06.512 --> 01:13:08.208
[pained grunting]

01:13:08.209 --> 01:13:10.080
[screams]

01:13:10.081 --> 01:13:12.213
[Other Mommy roaring]

01:13:12.823 --> 01:13:13.954
[screams]

01:13:15.303 --> 01:13:16.521
Come on! [grunts]

01:13:16.522 --> 01:13:17.783
[groans]

01:13:17.784 --> 01:13:19.524
Bela, Bela.

01:13:19.525 --> 01:13:21.134
- [growling]
- Oh!

01:13:21.135 --> 01:13:22.309
Down in the basement.

01:13:22.310 --> 01:13:24.574
Go! Go!

01:13:27.011 --> 01:13:28.403
OTHER MOMMY [distorted]:
Don't let them

01:13:28.404 --> 01:13:30.405
break your heart, Bela.

01:13:30.406 --> 01:13:33.016
- [rumbling]
- [light bulbs popping]

01:13:33.017 --> 01:13:34.583
BELA:
Mommy!

01:13:34.584 --> 01:13:36.586
[Mommy and Daddo grunting]

01:13:38.239 --> 01:13:39.805
[gasping]

01:13:39.806 --> 01:13:41.068
What do we do now?!

01:13:42.069 --> 01:13:43.635
We have to tell her!

01:13:43.636 --> 01:13:45.725
The innocence bullshit?!
That's not gonna work!

01:13:46.639 --> 01:13:48.727
[growling]

01:13:48.728 --> 01:13:50.076
Okay!

01:13:50.077 --> 01:13:51.904
Okay, do it!

01:13:51.905 --> 01:13:53.516
Do it!

01:13:56.475 --> 01:13:58.477
[audio continues muffled]

01:13:59.565 --> 01:14:01.698
♪ ♪

01:14:05.702 --> 01:14:08.792
I was married to someone else
when I got pregnant.

01:14:11.403 --> 01:14:14.014
<i>I wasn't planning
on having a child.</i>

01:14:16.974 --> 01:14:18.976
<i>I wasn't planning on anything.</i>

01:14:23.110 --> 01:14:27.113
And that's when I met Daddo.

01:14:27.114 --> 01:14:29.768
Oh, but he made me laugh.
Oh, he made me laugh.

01:14:29.769 --> 01:14:32.511
[laughing]:
Not-not the fake kind, you know?

01:14:34.557 --> 01:14:36.254
The real kind.

01:14:37.647 --> 01:14:40.344
And it caught me off guard.

01:14:40.345 --> 01:14:41.998
And I thought,

01:14:41.999 --> 01:14:44.043
"Oh, maybe I could...

01:14:44.044 --> 01:14:46.393
I could s--
I could start again."

01:14:46.394 --> 01:14:49.005
[muffled rumbling]

01:14:49.006 --> 01:14:51.921
And then when we found out
I was pregnant,

01:14:51.922 --> 01:14:53.576
we both cried, but...

01:14:55.055 --> 01:14:57.274
...not for the same reason.

01:14:57.275 --> 01:14:59.538
♪ ♪

01:15:04.543 --> 01:15:06.719
Daddo is not
your real father, Bela.

01:15:09.853 --> 01:15:11.506
[sobs softly]

01:15:11.507 --> 01:15:13.420
But he stayed.

01:15:13.421 --> 01:15:15.423
[muffled rumbling]

01:15:16.555 --> 01:15:18.252
Oh, he wanted you.

01:15:19.297 --> 01:15:21.864
He wanted to be a father.

01:15:21.865 --> 01:15:23.169
[door closing echoes]

01:15:23.170 --> 01:15:24.431
And I...

01:15:24.432 --> 01:15:26.478
[muffled rumbling fades]

01:15:33.137 --> 01:15:35.878
I didn't know how to say
that I didn't.

01:15:35.879 --> 01:15:38.795
[sobs softly]

01:15:41.624 --> 01:15:44.147
I never wanted to be a mother.

01:15:44.148 --> 01:15:46.193
♪ ♪

01:15:49.457 --> 01:15:51.459
Oh, I wanted to be free.

01:15:56.508 --> 01:15:57.943
Not because I didn't love you.

01:15:57.944 --> 01:15:59.945
[sobbing]:
Oh, God, I do.

01:15:59.946 --> 01:16:01.557
I love you.

01:16:03.036 --> 01:16:06.604
But because loving you meant
losing pieces of myself

01:16:06.605 --> 01:16:08.824
that I wasn't ready to give up.

01:16:08.825 --> 01:16:10.173
[sobbing]

01:16:10.174 --> 01:16:11.697
I'm sorry.

01:16:13.960 --> 01:16:16.919
For the lie. For all of it.

01:16:16.920 --> 01:16:20.400
For not being the kind of
mother you deserve.

01:16:20.401 --> 01:16:21.577
[sniffles]

01:16:22.534 --> 01:16:24.231
But that's it.

01:16:27.234 --> 01:16:29.280
That's finally the truth.

01:16:31.935 --> 01:16:34.110
[lights clicking]

01:16:34.111 --> 01:16:35.591
[panting]

01:16:40.639 --> 01:16:41.857
BELA:
No!

01:16:41.858 --> 01:16:43.946
- [sobbing]
- Oh. -MOMMY: Bela.

01:16:43.947 --> 01:16:44.990
[pained groan]

01:16:44.991 --> 01:16:46.296
I hate you!

01:16:46.297 --> 01:16:47.689
[panting]

01:16:47.690 --> 01:16:50.300
Bela. Bela.

01:16:50.301 --> 01:16:51.824
I'm still your Daddo.

01:16:52.869 --> 01:16:55.044
No, you're not.

01:16:55.045 --> 01:16:56.262
MOMMY:
No. No!

01:16:56.263 --> 01:16:58.351
It's not safe. It's not safe!

01:16:58.352 --> 01:16:59.701
[rumbling]

01:16:59.702 --> 01:17:02.138
[door echoes]

01:17:02.139 --> 01:17:04.184
[crying softly]

01:17:14.325 --> 01:17:15.934
[door opens]

01:17:15.935 --> 01:17:17.675
[door creaking]

01:17:17.676 --> 01:17:20.243
♪ ♪

01:17:20.244 --> 01:17:22.289
[crying, sniffling]

01:17:26.032 --> 01:17:28.730
Y-You're still here?

01:17:28.731 --> 01:17:30.733
[crying]

01:17:34.388 --> 01:17:36.476
I'm sorry, Other Mommy.

01:17:36.477 --> 01:17:39.349
Please. I don't want to be here.

01:17:39.350 --> 01:17:41.961
I'll say yes. Please!

01:17:42.962 --> 01:17:45.877
I'm ready, I swear.

01:17:45.878 --> 01:17:47.313
Please, Other Mommy.

01:17:47.314 --> 01:17:49.360
♪ ♪

01:17:55.105 --> 01:17:57.107
[eerie voices whispering]

01:18:03.200 --> 01:18:04.723
[glass squeaking softly]

01:18:10.424 --> 01:18:12.599
Please, Other Mommy.

01:18:12.600 --> 01:18:14.645
I'll do anything.

01:18:14.646 --> 01:18:16.692
Just don't leave me alone.

01:18:21.305 --> 01:18:22.349
[sniffles]

01:18:23.307 --> 01:18:24.742
[gasps]

01:18:24.743 --> 01:18:26.745
[panting]

01:18:40.150 --> 01:18:42.892
[voice echoing]: Maybe there's
something left to save.

01:18:47.157 --> 01:18:49.550
[voice echoing]: I didn't think
it would be this hard.

01:18:51.552 --> 01:18:54.119
It's so much easier
where I'm from.

01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:56.034
You'll like it there.

01:18:56.035 --> 01:18:58.341
What do I have to do?

01:18:58.342 --> 01:19:00.474
Just a hug.

01:19:03.260 --> 01:19:05.088
And you say yes.

01:19:07.351 --> 01:19:09.396
♪ ♪

01:19:18.449 --> 01:19:21.712
Bela, can I go
inside your heart?

01:19:21.713 --> 01:19:22.887
I'm scared.

01:19:22.888 --> 01:19:24.933
Shh.

01:19:24.934 --> 01:19:28.720
I'll make sure
nobody ever hurts you again.

01:19:29.852 --> 01:19:31.461
<i>[Grandma Ruth laughs]</i>

01:19:31.462 --> 01:19:34.987
Well, that's the biggest lie
of all, isn't it?

01:19:36.380 --> 01:19:38.250
[waves crashing]

01:19:38.251 --> 01:19:41.777
Nobody gets through life
without a few scars, Bela.

01:19:43.256 --> 01:19:47.869
You get to pick who you want
to let into your heart

01:19:47.870 --> 01:19:50.132
and who you want to keep out.

01:19:50.133 --> 01:19:52.830
That's what makes us powerful.

01:19:52.831 --> 01:19:54.702
That's being human.

01:19:56.313 --> 01:19:59.185
OTHER MOMMY:
You'll never be sad like them.

01:20:02.275 --> 01:20:04.059
[eerie voices whispering]

01:20:04.060 --> 01:20:06.278
You'll never be a liar
like them.

01:20:06.279 --> 01:20:07.498
[skin crackling]

01:20:09.979 --> 01:20:12.198
But I am a liar like them.

01:20:13.373 --> 01:20:14.939
I don't want you!

01:20:14.940 --> 01:20:16.812
I choose no!

01:20:17.856 --> 01:20:20.379
[rumbling]

01:20:20.380 --> 01:20:22.338
[heavy thud echoes]

01:20:22.339 --> 01:20:24.079
No, Other Mommy.

01:20:24.080 --> 01:20:25.950
[light bulbs clicking]

01:20:25.951 --> 01:20:28.561
[Other Mommy laughing]

01:20:28.562 --> 01:20:30.868
OTHER MOMMY:
You stupid,

01:20:30.869 --> 01:20:34.002
broken child.

01:20:34.003 --> 01:20:36.005
[crackling]

01:20:41.575 --> 01:20:43.621
[wheezing]

01:20:46.058 --> 01:20:48.930
[laughing]

01:20:48.931 --> 01:20:50.933
[raspy growling]

01:20:54.719 --> 01:20:55.938
[grunts]

01:20:57.504 --> 01:20:58.766
[chuckles]

01:21:03.336 --> 01:21:06.687
They'll never love you
like I did, Bela.

01:21:08.689 --> 01:21:10.822
- No, Other Mommy!
- [crackling, pained gasping]

01:21:11.997 --> 01:21:14.129
- No!
- [pained groaning]

01:21:14.130 --> 01:21:15.957
- No!
- [pained grunt]

01:21:15.958 --> 01:21:18.611
[wheezing]

01:21:18.612 --> 01:21:20.658
[gasping]

01:21:25.184 --> 01:21:29.188
Every time you look at her,
you'll think of me.

01:21:36.761 --> 01:21:38.806
[low growling]

01:21:41.809 --> 01:21:47.250
[whispering]:
You can play happy family.

01:21:49.034 --> 01:21:52.341
But it'll just be pretend.

01:21:52.342 --> 01:21:54.953
[whispering]:
Good night, Other Mommy.

01:21:58.783 --> 01:22:00.784
- [yells]
- [squelching]

01:22:00.785 --> 01:22:02.481
[whooshing]

01:22:02.482 --> 01:22:04.875
- [sharp squelching]
- [howling]

01:22:04.876 --> 01:22:06.572
[wind whistling]

01:22:06.573 --> 01:22:09.575
[eerie voices whispering]

01:22:09.576 --> 01:22:12.491
OTHER MOMMY [faintly]:
Bela! Bela!

01:22:12.492 --> 01:22:14.538
[howling]

01:22:19.673 --> 01:22:20.891
[howling stops]

01:22:20.892 --> 01:22:22.938
[panting]

01:22:24.678 --> 01:22:25.765
[Daddo and Mommy panting]

01:22:25.766 --> 01:22:27.419
- Mommy!
- Oh, God.

01:22:27.420 --> 01:22:29.466
[panting]

01:22:31.642 --> 01:22:32.990
MOMMY:
We'll fix it.

01:22:32.991 --> 01:22:34.600
We'll fix it, Bela.

01:22:34.601 --> 01:22:35.994
There's no more lies.

01:22:39.824 --> 01:22:41.478
[whispers]:
Daddo.

01:22:43.001 --> 01:22:45.221
[crying]

01:22:50.574 --> 01:22:52.619
♪ ♪

01:22:54.621 --> 01:22:56.667
[soft whooshing]

01:22:58.799 --> 01:23:00.845
[soft tinkling]

01:23:11.203 --> 01:23:13.509
BELA:
<i>Hello and good morning.</i>

01:23:13.510 --> 01:23:16.512
<i>My name is Isabela Martin,</i>

01:23:16.513 --> 01:23:21.517
<i>and this is "The Story of Me."</i>

01:23:21.518 --> 01:23:26.262
<i>I'm very excited to make new
friends this year at school.</i>

01:23:29.613 --> 01:23:32.485
<i>There's a song I used to sing
about friends.</i>

01:23:33.573 --> 01:23:36.271
<i>It says,
"New friends are silver.</i>

01:23:36.272 --> 01:23:39.144
<i>Old friends are gold."</i>

01:23:43.018 --> 01:23:45.107
<i>All my old friends are gone.</i>

01:23:50.112 --> 01:23:52.114
♪ ♪

01:24:02.037 --> 01:24:04.995
<i>I'm not allowed
to talk about my summer.</i>

01:24:04.996 --> 01:24:09.652
<i>The police finally stopped
coming to our house.</i>

01:24:09.653 --> 01:24:12.916
<i>- I live with my mom and dad...</i>
- [Daddo and Mommy chattering]

01:24:12.917 --> 01:24:16.267
<i>...Ursula Martin
and Russell Martin.</i>

01:24:16.268 --> 01:24:20.706
<i>Something special about me
is my zipper.</i>

01:24:20.707 --> 01:24:22.708
<i>My mom has one, too.</i>

01:24:22.709 --> 01:24:24.536
- DADDO: All right.
- MOMMY: Hey, honey.

01:24:24.537 --> 01:24:25.842
Does it still hurt?

01:24:25.843 --> 01:24:28.366
Oh, God, no. It just itches.

01:24:28.367 --> 01:24:31.195
How are you gonna tell people
you got yours?

01:24:31.196 --> 01:24:32.675
Well, I don't know.

01:24:32.676 --> 01:24:34.720
I guess I'm gonna
have to make something up.

01:24:34.721 --> 01:24:36.026
Okay, that looks good.

01:24:36.027 --> 01:24:37.767
BELA:
<i>My mom and my dad</i>

01:24:37.768 --> 01:24:39.595
<i>- love each other very much.</i>
- DADDO: Guess what.

01:24:39.596 --> 01:24:41.467
Everybody survived. Mwah.

01:24:44.209 --> 01:24:48.257
BELA:
<i>We are a very happy family.</i>

01:24:52.435 --> 01:24:55.438
["The Great Pretender" playing]

01:24:57.657 --> 01:24:59.702
♪ Oh, yes ♪

01:24:59.703 --> 01:25:03.358
♪ I'm the great pretender ♪

01:25:03.359 --> 01:25:04.837
<i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>

01:25:04.838 --> 01:25:09.799
♪ Pretending
that I'm doing well ♪

01:25:09.800 --> 01:25:10.930
<i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>

01:25:10.931 --> 01:25:13.890
♪ My need is such ♪

01:25:13.891 --> 01:25:17.198
♪ I pretend too much ♪

01:25:17.199 --> 01:25:21.855
♪ I'm lonely,
but no one can tell ♪

01:25:22.943 --> 01:25:25.031
♪ Oh, yes ♪

